window.I21_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"Fossil Fuels & Extraction 化石燃料與開採","cards":[{"w":"crude oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"oil in its natural state before it is cleaned","c":"原油","s":"The price of crude oil went up sharply last month, so many airlines raised their ticket prices for the summer holidays.","t":"上個月原油價格急劇上漲，所以許多航空公司調高了暑假的機票價格。"},{"w":"natural gas","p":"n.phr.","d":"a gas from under the ground used for heating and cooking","c":"天然氣","s":"Most homes in our city cook with natural gas, but some older buildings still use heavy gas bottles instead.","t":"我們城市大多數家庭用天然氣煮飯，但有些舊大樓仍然使用笨重的瓦斯桶。"},{"w":"oil field","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area where a lot of oil is under the ground","c":"油田","s":"Thousands of workers moved to the desert after a huge oil field was discovered, and a new town quickly grew there.","t":"在發現一座巨大的油田之後，數千名工人搬到沙漠，一座新城鎮很快就在那裡發展起來。"},{"w":"oil well","p":"n.phr.","d":"a deep hole made in the ground to get oil out","c":"油井","s":"The company drilled a new oil well near the coast, but local fishermen worried that a leak could harm the sea.","t":"這家公司在海岸附近鑽了一口新油井，但當地漁民擔心外洩可能會傷害海洋。"},{"w":"pipeline","p":"n.","d":"a long pipe that carries oil, gas or water far away","c":"輸送管線","s":"A new gas pipeline will run under the sea to our island, so we will no longer need to ship gas by boat.","t":"一條新的天然氣管線將從海底通到我們的島，所以我們將不再需要用船運送天然氣。"},{"w":"fracking","p":"n.","d":"pumping water into rocks to break them and release gas","c":"水力壓裂法","s":"Some countries have banned fracking because it uses huge amounts of water and may cause small earthquakes in nearby towns.","t":"有些國家已經禁止水力壓裂法，因為它使用大量的水，而且可能在附近城鎮引發小地震。"},{"w":"shale gas","p":"n.phr.","d":"natural gas trapped inside layers of soft rock","c":"頁岩氣","s":"The USA produces a lot of shale gas today, and this has made gas much cheaper for American factories and homes.","t":"美國現在生產大量的頁岩氣，這讓美國工廠和家庭的天然氣變得便宜許多。"},{"w":"tar sands","p":"n.phr.","d":"sand mixed with thick, sticky oil","c":"油砂","s":"Getting oil out of tar sands uses a lot of energy and water, so environmental groups say it is a very dirty process.","t":"從油砂中提煉石油會消耗大量能源和水，所以環保團體說這是非常骯髒的過程。"},{"w":"barrel","p":"n.","d":"a unit used to measure oil, about 159 litres","c":"桶（石油計量單位）","s":"The news reported that oil now costs over ninety dollars a barrel, and drivers are worried about paying more for petrol.","t":"新聞報導石油現在每桶超過九十美元，駕駛人擔心要付更多油錢。"},{"w":"petrol","p":"n.","d":"liquid fuel used in most cars","c":"汽油","s":"My dad always fills the car with petrol before a long trip, because there are few stations on the mountain road.","t":"我爸爸在長途旅行前總是先把車加滿汽油，因為山路上的加油站很少。"},{"w":"diesel","p":"n.","d":"a heavy fuel used in trucks, buses and some cars","c":"柴油","s":"Most big trucks run on diesel, but the city plans to replace its old buses with quieter electric ones next year.","t":"大多數大卡車使用柴油，但市政府計畫明年用更安靜的電動公車取代舊公車。"},{"w":"kerosene","p":"n.","d":"an oil burned in lamps and some heaters","c":"煤油","s":"During the typhoon the electricity went off, so my grandmother lit an old kerosene lamp and we played cards together.","t":"颱風期間停電了，所以奶奶點了一盞舊的煤油燈，我們一起玩牌。"},{"w":"jet fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"special fuel used by aeroplanes","c":"航空燃油","s":"Planes burn a huge amount of jet fuel on long flights, so airlines are testing cleaner fuels made from used cooking oil.","t":"飛機在長途飛行中燃燒大量的航空燃油，所以航空公司正在測試用廢食用油製成的更乾淨燃料。"},{"w":"liquefied natural gas","p":"n.phr.","d":"natural gas cooled until it becomes liquid for shipping","c":"液化天然氣","s":"Taiwan imports most of its gas as liquefied natural gas, which arrives in special ships and is stored in cold tanks.","t":"台灣進口的天然氣大多是液化天然氣，它由特殊船隻運來，並儲存在低溫儲槽中。"},{"w":"propane","p":"n.","d":"a gas sold in tanks for cooking and heating","c":"丙烷","s":"We took a small propane stove on our camping trip, and it was easy to cook noodles even in the rain.","t":"我們露營時帶了一個小型丙烷爐，即使在下雨也很容易煮麵。"},{"w":"oil tanker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large ship that carries oil","c":"油輪","s":"A huge oil tanker got stuck in the canal for six days, and many other ships had to wait outside.","t":"一艘巨大的油輪在運河中卡了六天，許多其他船隻只好在外面等候。"},{"w":"oil reserves","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of oil a country still has underground","c":"石油蘊藏量","s":"Saudi Arabia has some of the largest oil reserves in the world, so it has great power in the energy market.","t":"沙烏地阿拉伯擁有世界上最大的石油蘊藏量之一，所以它在能源市場上擁有很大的影響力。"},{"w":"lignite","p":"n.","d":"soft brown coal that produces a lot of smoke","c":"褐煤","s":"Burning lignite creates more pollution than other types of coal, but some power plants still use it because it is cheap.","t":"燃燒褐煤比其他種類的煤產生更多污染，但有些電廠仍使用它，因為它很便宜。"},{"w":"peak oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time when world oil production reaches its highest point","c":"石油產量頂峰","s":"Some experts believe we have already reached peak oil, while others think new technology will let us find more oil.","t":"有些專家認為我們已經到達石油產量頂峰，而其他人則認為新技術將讓我們找到更多石油。"},{"w":"gas flaring","p":"n.phr.","d":"burning off unwanted gas at an oil well","c":"天然氣燃除","s":"You can see huge flames at night because of gas flaring, and this wastes gas that could heat thousands of homes.","t":"由於天然氣燃除，你在夜晚可以看到巨大的火焰，而這浪費了足以供暖數千戶家庭的天然氣。"},{"w":"petrochemical","p":"adj.","d":"made from oil or natural gas","c":"石化的","s":"Many petrochemical factories line the southern coast, and people living nearby often complain about the bad smell in the air.","t":"許多石化工廠沿著南部海岸設立，住在附近的居民常常抱怨空氣中的難聞氣味。"},{"w":"refining","p":"n.","d":"the process of making oil clean and useful","c":"精煉","s":"After refining, crude oil can be turned into petrol, diesel and plastics, so the process is very important for industry.","t":"經過精煉之後，原油可以轉變成汽油、柴油和塑膠，所以這個過程對工業非常重要。"},{"w":"rig","p":"n.","d":"a large structure used to drill for oil or gas","c":"鑽油平台；鑽井設備","s":"My uncle works on a rig in the North Sea for two weeks at a time, and then he flies home to rest.","t":"我叔叔在北海的一座鑽油平台上一次工作兩週，然後再搭飛機回家休息。"},{"w":"derrick","p":"n.","d":"a tall metal tower built over an oil well","c":"井架","s":"An old oil derrick still stands in the town square, and tourists take photos of it to remember the town's history.","t":"一座舊的石油井架仍矗立在鎮上廣場，遊客會拍照留念這個城鎮的歷史。"},{"w":"oil platform","p":"n.phr.","d":"a structure in the sea where oil is taken from the seabed","c":"海上採油平台","s":"A storm hit the oil platform last night, so all the workers were flown back to land by helicopter.","t":"昨晚一場暴風雨襲擊了海上採油平台，所以所有工人都被直升機載回陸地。"},{"w":"petrol station","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where you buy fuel for your car","c":"加油站","s":"We stopped at a petrol station to fill the tank, and my little brother bought some snacks from the shop there.","t":"我們在加油站停下來加滿油，我弟弟在那裡的商店買了一些零食。"},{"w":"heating oil","p":"n.phr.","d":"oil burned to keep buildings warm","c":"暖氣用油","s":"Many families in the countryside buy heating oil every autumn, because the winters there are long and very cold.","t":"許多鄉下家庭每年秋天都會購買暖氣用油，因為那裡的冬天又長又冷。"},{"w":"oil exploration","p":"n.phr.","d":"searching for new places where oil can be found","c":"石油探勘","s":"The government allowed oil exploration near the national park, but many citizens protested because they wanted to protect the wildlife.","t":"政府允許在國家公園附近進行石油探勘，但許多市民抗議，因為他們想要保護野生動物。"},{"w":"gas leak","p":"n.phr.","d":"gas escaping by accident from a pipe","c":"瓦斯外洩","s":"We smelled something strange in the kitchen, so we opened all the windows and called the company to check for a gas leak.","t":"我們在廚房聞到奇怪的味道，所以打開所有窗戶，並打電話請公司來檢查是否有瓦斯外洩。"},{"w":"oil slick","p":"n.phr.","d":"a layer of oil floating on the sea","c":"浮油","s":"A large oil slick spread along the beach after the accident, and volunteers spent weeks cleaning oil off seabirds.","t":"事故發生後，一大片浮油沿著海灘擴散，志工們花了好幾週清理海鳥身上的油汙。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"Electricity & the Power Grid 電力與電網","cards":[{"w":"power plant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a factory that produces electricity","c":"發電廠","s":"The new power plant will supply electricity to half a million homes, but people living nearby are worried about the noise.","t":"這座新發電廠將供電給五十萬戶家庭，但住在附近的人擔心噪音問題。"},{"w":"power line","p":"n.phr.","d":"a wire that carries electricity over long distances","c":"電線；輸電線","s":"A fallen tree broke a power line during the storm, so our whole street had no electricity until the next morning.","t":"暴風雨期間一棵倒下的樹弄斷了一條電線，所以我們整條街直到隔天早上都沒有電。"},{"w":"pylon","p":"n.","d":"a tall metal tower that holds up power lines","c":"電塔","s":"Workers are building a giant pylon on the hill, and it will carry electricity from the wind farm to the city.","t":"工人們正在山丘上建造一座巨大的電塔，它將把風力發電場的電輸送到城市。"},{"w":"transformer","p":"n.","d":"a device that changes the voltage of electricity","c":"變壓器","s":"The transformer outside our building exploded with a loud bang, so the lifts stopped and everyone had to use the stairs.","t":"我們大樓外的變壓器發出巨響爆炸了，所以電梯停了，大家只好走樓梯。"},{"w":"substation","p":"n.","d":"a place where electricity is changed before reaching homes","c":"變電所","s":"The power company is building a substation near our school, but parents want to know whether it is completely safe.","t":"電力公司正在我們學校附近興建一座變電所，但家長們想知道它是否完全安全。"},{"w":"power cut","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when the electricity supply stops","c":"停電","s":"There was a power cut in the middle of my online exam, so I had to explain the problem to my teacher by phone.","t":"我線上考試考到一半時停電了，所以我只好打電話向老師解釋問題。"},{"w":"blackout","p":"n.","d":"a time when a whole area loses electricity","c":"大停電","s":"The heatwave caused a huge blackout across the city, and traffic lights stopped working during the busy evening rush hour.","t":"熱浪造成全市大停電，交通號誌在繁忙的傍晚尖峰時段都停止運作。"},{"w":"outage","p":"n.","d":"a period when a service like electricity stops working","c":"停電；中斷","s":"The company apologised for the two-hour outage, and it promised to give every customer a small discount on next month's bill.","t":"公司為長達兩小時的停電道歉，並承諾下個月的帳單給每位客戶小額折扣。"},{"w":"peak demand","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time when people use the most electricity","c":"尖峰用電需求","s":"peak demand usually happens on hot summer afternoons, because almost every office and home turns on the air conditioning.","t":"尖峰用電需求通常發生在炎熱的夏日午後，因為幾乎每間辦公室和住家都會開冷氣。"},{"w":"off-peak","p":"adj.","d":"at a time when fewer people use something, so it is cheaper","c":"離峰的","s":"We run the washing machine at night because off-peak electricity is cheaper, and it helps us save money every month.","t":"我們在晚上使用洗衣機，因為離峰電價比較便宜，這幫助我們每個月省錢。"},{"w":"baseload","p":"n.","d":"the minimum amount of power needed all the time","c":"基載電力","s":"Coal plants used to supply most of the baseload, but now gas and nuclear plants provide more of this steady power.","t":"燃煤電廠過去提供大部分的基載電力，但現在燃氣和核能電廠提供更多這種穩定的電力。"},{"w":"kilowatt","p":"n.","d":"a unit of power equal to 1,000 watts","c":"千瓦","s":"This small heater uses about one kilowatt of power, so it can warm a bedroom without making the bill too high.","t":"這台小型暖氣機大約耗電一千瓦，所以它可以讓臥室變暖又不會讓電費太高。"},{"w":"kilowatt-hour","p":"n.","d":"a unit of electricity used, shown on your bill","c":"千瓦時；度","s":"Electricity costs about four dollars per kilowatt-hour in summer, so my mum asks us to turn off lights we are not using.","t":"夏天每度電大約四元，所以媽媽要我們關掉沒在用的燈。"},{"w":"megawatt","p":"n.","d":"a unit of power equal to one million watts","c":"百萬瓦；兆瓦","s":"Each of the new wind turbines can produce eight megawatt, and together they will power thousands of homes on the coast.","t":"每一座新的風力發電機都能產生八百萬瓦的電力，合起來將供電給沿海的數千戶家庭。"},{"w":"watt","p":"n.","d":"a basic unit for measuring electric power","c":"瓦特","s":"This LED bulb uses only ten watt, but it gives as much light as an old bulb that used sixty.","t":"這顆LED燈泡只用十瓦，但它的亮度和舊的六十瓦燈泡一樣。"},{"w":"alternating current","p":"n.phr.","d":"electricity that changes direction many times a second","c":"交流電","s":"Homes are supplied with alternating current, but phones and laptops need an adapter because they run on direct current.","t":"家庭供應的是交流電，但手機和筆電需要變壓器，因為它們使用直流電。"},{"w":"socket","p":"n.","d":"the place in a wall where you plug things in","c":"插座","s":"There is only one socket next to my bed, so I use an extension cord to charge my phone and lamp.","t":"我床邊只有一個插座，所以我用延長線來替手機充電和接檯燈。"},{"w":"plug","p":"n.","d":"the part at the end of a wire that goes into a socket","c":"插頭","s":"British plug have three square pins, so we bought a travel adapter before our trip to London.","t":"英國的插頭有三根方形插腳，所以我們在去倫敦前買了一個旅行轉接頭。"},{"w":"extension cord","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long wire that lets you plug in things far from a socket","c":"延長線","s":"Never connect too many heaters to one extension cord, because it can get very hot and may even start a fire.","t":"千萬不要在一條延長線上接太多暖氣機，因為它會變得很燙，甚至可能引起火災。"},{"w":"power strip","p":"n.phr.","d":"a row of sockets on a short cable","c":"排插","s":"I plug my computer, printer and lamp into one power strip, so I can switch them all off with one button.","t":"我把電腦、印表機和檯燈都插在一個排插上，這樣我只要按一個按鈕就能全部關掉。"},{"w":"circuit breaker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a switch that stops electricity when there is a problem","c":"斷路器","s":"When we used the oven and the heater together, the circuit breaker switched off, and the whole kitchen went dark.","t":"當我們同時使用烤箱和暖氣機時，斷路器跳掉了，整個廚房一片漆黑。"},{"w":"short circuit","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fault where electricity takes the wrong path","c":"短路","s":"Water got into the old hair dryer and caused a short circuit, so there was a spark and a smell of burning plastic.","t":"水跑進那台舊吹風機造成短路，所以冒出火花，還有塑膠燒焦的味道。"},{"w":"electrical","p":"adj.","d":"related to or using electricity","c":"電的；電氣的","s":"The fire was caused by an electrical fault in the old building, so the owner has now replaced all the wiring.","t":"這場火災是舊大樓的電氣故障所引起的，所以屋主現在已經更換了所有電線。"},{"w":"utility company","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that supplies electricity, gas or water","c":"公用事業公司","s":"The utility company sent a letter about higher prices, but it also offered tips on how families can use less power.","t":"公用事業公司寄來一封關於漲價的信，但也提供了家庭如何少用電的小技巧。"},{"w":"transmission line","p":"n.phr.","d":"a high-voltage cable that carries power across a country","c":"輸電線路","s":"A new transmission line will carry solar power from the south to the north, because most factories are in the north.","t":"一條新的輸電線路將把太陽能電力從南部送到北部，因為大部分工廠都在北部。"},{"w":"power supply","p":"n.phr.","d":"the electricity that is provided to a place","c":"電力供應","s":"Hospitals need a steady power supply all the time, so they keep large backup generators in case the main electricity fails.","t":"醫院隨時都需要穩定的電力供應，所以他們備有大型備用發電機，以防主電源中斷。"},{"w":"surge protector","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that protects machines from sudden strong electricity","c":"突波保護器","s":"Lightning hit our neighbourhood last night, but my computer was fine because it was plugged into a surge protector.","t":"昨晚閃電打中我們社區，但我的電腦沒事，因為它插在突波保護器上。"},{"w":"smart grid","p":"n.phr.","d":"an electricity network that uses computers to manage power","c":"智慧電網","s":"A smart grid can send power where it is needed most, so it reduces waste and helps prevent sudden blackouts.","t":"智慧電網能把電力送到最需要的地方，所以它減少浪費，並幫助防止突然大停電。"},{"w":"microgrid","p":"n.","d":"a small local power network that can work alone","c":"微電網","s":"The island village built its own microgrid with solar panels and batteries, so it no longer depends on the main power network.","t":"這個島上的村莊用太陽能板和電池建造了自己的微電網，所以不再依賴主要電網。"},{"w":"rolling blackout","p":"n.phr.","d":"planned power cuts that move from area to area","c":"輪流停電","s":"During the energy shortage, the city used rolling blackout to save power, so each district lost electricity for two hours.","t":"能源短缺期間，城市實施輪流停電來節省電力，所以每個區域停電兩小時。"},{"w":"electrify","p":"v.","d":"to supply something with electricity","c":"使電氣化；供電給","s":"The government plans to electrify all the railways by 2035, because electric trains are cleaner and quieter than diesel ones.","t":"政府計畫在2035年前將所有鐵路電氣化，因為電動火車比柴油火車更乾淨也更安靜。"},{"w":"load shedding","p":"n.phr.","d":"cutting power to some areas so the system does not fail","c":"限電；分區停電","s":"South Africa has suffered from load shedding for years, so many shops now keep their own generators to stay open.","t":"南非多年來一直受限電之苦，所以許多商店現在自備發電機以維持營業。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"Renewable Energy 再生能源","cards":[{"w":"solar farm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large area of land covered with solar panels","c":"太陽能發電場","s":"The old salt fields were turned into a solar farm, and now they produce clean electricity for nearby towns.","t":"舊鹽田被改建成太陽能發電場，現在為附近城鎮生產乾淨的電力。"},{"w":"solar power","p":"n.phr.","d":"electricity made from sunlight","c":"太陽能發電","s":"Our school has started using solar power on its roof, and the electricity bill has dropped by almost a third.","t":"我們學校已經開始在屋頂使用太陽能發電，電費幾乎減少了三分之一。"},{"w":"solar cell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small device that changes sunlight into electricity","c":"太陽能電池","s":"My calculator has a tiny solar cell above the screen, so I never need to change its battery.","t":"我的計算機螢幕上方有一個小小的太陽能電池，所以我從來不需要換電池。"},{"w":"solar water heater","p":"n.phr.","d":"a system on a roof that uses the sun to heat water","c":"太陽能熱水器","s":"My grandparents installed a solar water heater on their roof, and now they can take hot showers without using gas.","t":"我祖父母在屋頂裝了太陽能熱水器，現在他們不用瓦斯就能洗熱水澡。"},{"w":"rooftop solar","p":"n.phr.","d":"solar panels placed on the roofs of buildings","c":"屋頂型太陽能","s":"More families are choosing rooftop solar because it lowers their bills, and they can sell extra power back to the grid.","t":"越來越多家庭選擇屋頂型太陽能，因為它能降低電費，而且他們可以把多餘的電賣回電網。"},{"w":"wind farm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of wind turbines that make electricity","c":"風力發電場","s":"We could see a wind farm from the beach, and the tall white turbines were turning slowly in the sea breeze.","t":"我們從海灘上可以看見一座風力發電場，高大的白色風機在海風中緩緩轉動。"},{"w":"offshore wind farm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of wind turbines built in the sea","c":"離岸風場","s":"Taiwan is building many offshore wind farm in the Taiwan Strait, because the wind there is strong for most of the year.","t":"台灣正在台灣海峽興建許多離岸風場，因為那裡一年大部分時間風都很強。"},{"w":"wind power","p":"n.phr.","d":"electricity made by the movement of wind","c":"風力發電","s":"Denmark gets about half of its electricity from wind power, so it is often used as a model for other countries.","t":"丹麥大約一半的電力來自風力發電，所以它經常被當作其他國家的典範。"},{"w":"blade","p":"n.","d":"one of the long flat parts of a turbine that turns","c":"葉片","s":"Each blade of the turbine is longer than a football field, so it must be carried to the coast on a special truck.","t":"風機的每一片葉片都比足球場還長，所以必須用特殊卡車運到海岸。"},{"w":"rotor","p":"n.","d":"the turning part of a machine","c":"轉子；旋翼","s":"The engineer stopped the rotor because the wind was too strong, and he did not want the machine to be damaged.","t":"工程師讓轉子停下來，因為風太強了，他不希望機器受損。"},{"w":"hydroelectric","p":"adj.","d":"producing electricity from moving water","c":"水力發電的","s":"The hydroelectric station in the mountains uses water from the river, and it can quickly increase power when demand is high.","t":"山區的水力發電廠利用河水，當需求高時它能迅速增加發電量。"},{"w":"dam","p":"n.","d":"a wall built across a river to hold back water","c":"水壩","s":"The new dam will store water for farmers and produce electricity, but hundreds of families must move away from the valley.","t":"新水壩將為農民儲水並發電，但數百戶家庭必須搬離山谷。"},{"w":"tidal power","p":"n.phr.","d":"electricity made from the rise and fall of the sea","c":"潮汐發電","s":"tidal power is very predictable because tides come at fixed times, but building the machines in the sea is expensive.","t":"潮汐發電非常容易預測，因為潮汐在固定時間出現，但在海中建造機器很昂貴。"},{"w":"wave energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"power taken from the movement of ocean waves","c":"波浪能","s":"Scientists are testing machines that collect wave energy off the coast, and they hope the idea will work on a large scale.","t":"科學家正在海岸外測試收集波浪能的機器，他們希望這個構想能大規模運作。"},{"w":"biogas","p":"n.","d":"gas made from rotting food, plants or animal waste","c":"沼氣","s":"The pig farm turns animal waste into biogas, so it can heat its own buildings and reduce bad smells at the same time.","t":"這座養豬場把動物排泄物轉變成沼氣，所以既能為自己的建築供暖，同時也能減少臭味。"},{"w":"ethanol","p":"n.","d":"an alcohol made from plants that can be used as fuel","c":"乙醇","s":"In Brazil many cars run on ethanol made from sugar cane, so the country needs less imported oil.","t":"在巴西，許多車使用由甘蔗製成的乙醇，所以這個國家需要進口的石油較少。"},{"w":"biodiesel","p":"n.","d":"a fuel made from vegetable oil or animal fat","c":"生質柴油","s":"Our city's rubbish trucks now use biodiesel made from used cooking oil, and the air around the stations smells less of smoke.","t":"我們城市的垃圾車現在使用廢食用油製成的生質柴油，車站周圍的空氣也比較沒有煙味了。"},{"w":"green hydrogen","p":"n.phr.","d":"hydrogen made using renewable electricity","c":"綠氫","s":"Steel companies are interested in green hydrogen, because it could replace coal and cut a huge amount of pollution.","t":"鋼鐵公司對綠氫很感興趣，因為它可能取代煤炭並大幅減少污染。"},{"w":"fuel cell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that makes electricity from hydrogen and oxygen","c":"燃料電池","s":"This bus runs on a hydrogen fuel cell, and the only thing that comes out of the back is clean water.","t":"這輛公車使用氫燃料電池，從車尾排出的唯一東西就是乾淨的水。"},{"w":"hydrogen","p":"n.","d":"a very light gas that can be used as clean fuel","c":"氫","s":"Japan wants to use more hydrogen in the future, because burning it produces water instead of harmful gases.","t":"日本未來想使用更多氫，因為燃燒它產生的是水，而不是有害氣體。"},{"w":"clean energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"power that causes little or no pollution","c":"乾淨能源","s":"Many young people want to work in clean energy, because they believe it is good for the planet and has a bright future.","t":"許多年輕人想在乾淨能源領域工作，因為他們相信這對地球有益，而且前途光明。"},{"w":"alternative energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"energy that does not come from fossil fuels","c":"替代能源","s":"Our class did a project on alternative energy, and each group built a small model powered by the sun or wind.","t":"我們班做了一個關於替代能源的專題，每一組都做了一個靠太陽或風驅動的小模型。"},{"w":"renewables","p":"n.","d":"energy sources such as sun and wind that never run out","c":"再生能源","s":"The share of electricity from renewables has grown quickly, but coal and gas are still the main sources in many countries.","t":"來自再生能源的電力比例快速成長，但在許多國家煤和天然氣仍是主要來源。"},{"w":"intermittency","p":"n.","d":"the problem of not producing power all the time","c":"間歇性","s":"The biggest problem with solar power is intermittency, because panels produce nothing at night and very little on cloudy days.","t":"太陽能最大的問題是間歇性，因為太陽能板在夜間完全不發電，陰天也發電很少。"},{"w":"energy transition","p":"n.phr.","d":"the change from fossil fuels to clean energy","c":"能源轉型","s":"The energy transition will create many new jobs, but workers in coal towns are afraid that they will be left behind.","t":"能源轉型將創造許多新工作，但煤礦城鎮的工人擔心他們會被拋在後頭。"},{"w":"feed-in tariff","p":"n.phr.","d":"a fixed price paid for clean power sold to the grid","c":"躉購費率","s":"The government offers a generous feed-in tariff, so farmers can earn money by putting solar panels on their fish ponds.","t":"政府提供優厚的躉購費率，所以農民可以在魚塭上裝設太陽能板來賺錢。"},{"w":"solar-powered","p":"adj.","d":"using energy from the sun","c":"太陽能驅動的","s":"We bought a solar-powered lamp for the garden, and it charges during the day and turns on by itself at night.","t":"我們買了一盞太陽能花園燈，它白天充電，晚上會自己亮起來。"},{"w":"inverter","p":"n.","d":"a device that changes direct current into alternating current","c":"逆變器","s":"The solar panels on our roof stopped working because the inverter was broken, so the technician came to replace it.","t":"我們屋頂的太陽能板停止運作，因為逆變器壞了，所以技術人員來更換。"},{"w":"sunlight","p":"n.","d":"the light that comes from the sun","c":"陽光","s":"Southern Taiwan gets plenty of sunlight all year round, so it is a good place to build large solar projects.","t":"台灣南部全年都有充足的陽光，所以是建造大型太陽能計畫的好地點。"},{"w":"wind speed","p":"n.phr.","d":"how fast the wind is blowing","c":"風速","s":"The turbines only start turning when the wind speed is high enough, so on calm days they produce no power at all.","t":"風機只有在風速夠高時才會開始轉動，所以在無風的日子完全不發電。"},{"w":"spillway","p":"n.","d":"a channel that lets extra water flow out of a dam","c":"溢洪道","s":"After days of heavy rain, the spillway was opened to release water, and crowds gathered to watch the powerful flow.","t":"連續數日豪雨之後，溢洪道被打開洩洪，群眾聚集觀看強大的水流。"},{"w":"run-of-river","p":"adj.","d":"using a river's natural flow without a big dam","c":"川流式的","s":"A small run-of-river power station was built on the stream, so the village gets electricity without flooding the valley.","t":"小溪上建了一座小型川流式發電站，所以村莊不必淹沒山谷就能取得電力。"},{"w":"installed capacity","p":"n.phr.","d":"the maximum power that all machines can produce","c":"裝置容量","s":"The country's installed capacity for solar power has doubled in five years, but actual output depends on the weather.","t":"這個國家的太陽能裝置容量五年內增加了一倍，但實際發電量取決於天氣。"},{"w":"capacity factor","p":"n.phr.","d":"how much power a plant really makes compared with its maximum","c":"容量因數","s":"Offshore turbines have a higher capacity factor than those on land, because the wind at sea is stronger and steadier.","t":"離岸風機的容量因數比陸上風機高，因為海上的風更強也更穩定。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"Nuclear Power 核能","cards":[{"w":"nuclear power plant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a power station that uses nuclear reactions","c":"核能發電廠","s":"The last nuclear power plant in Taiwan was shut down in 2025, but people are still debating whether to restart it.","t":"台灣最後一座核能發電廠在2025年停機，但人們仍在爭論是否要重新啟用。"},{"w":"nuclear reactor","p":"n.phr.","d":"the machine in which nuclear energy is produced","c":"核子反應爐","s":"The nuclear reactor is kept inside a thick concrete building, so radiation cannot escape even if there is an accident.","t":"核子反應爐被安置在厚重的混凝土建築內，所以即使發生事故，輻射也無法外洩。"},{"w":"uranium","p":"n.","d":"a heavy metal used as fuel in nuclear power","c":"鈾","s":"Australia has large amounts of uranium, and it sells this metal to countries that run nuclear power stations.","t":"澳洲擁有大量的鈾，並把這種金屬賣給經營核電廠的國家。"},{"w":"plutonium","p":"n.","d":"a dangerous metal made in nuclear reactors","c":"鈽","s":"plutonium can stay dangerous for thousands of years, so it must be stored under strict security.","t":"鈽可以維持危險性長達數千年，所以必須在嚴格的安全措施下儲存。"},{"w":"fission","p":"n.","d":"the splitting of an atom, which releases energy","c":"核分裂","s":"Nuclear power stations use fission to produce heat, and this heat turns water into steam that drives the turbines.","t":"核電廠利用核分裂產生熱能，而這些熱把水變成蒸汽來推動渦輪機。"},{"w":"nuclear waste","p":"n.phr.","d":"dangerous material left after making nuclear power","c":"核廢料","s":"Nobody wants to live near a store of nuclear waste, so finding a safe place to keep it is very difficult.","t":"沒有人想住在核廢料儲存場附近，所以要找到安全的存放地點非常困難。"},{"w":"radioactive","p":"adj.","d":"giving off harmful energy from atoms","c":"有放射性的","s":"The workers wore special suits because the area was radioactive, and they could only stay inside for a few minutes.","t":"工人們穿著特殊防護衣，因為這個區域具有放射性，他們只能在裡面待幾分鐘。"},{"w":"meltdown","p":"n.","d":"a serious accident when a nuclear reactor overheats","c":"爐心熔毀","s":"After the earthquake, there was a meltdown at the power station, and thousands of people had to leave their homes.","t":"地震之後，電廠發生了爐心熔毀，數千人必須離開家園。"},{"w":"nuclear accident","p":"n.phr.","d":"an event that releases harmful radiation by mistake","c":"核子事故","s":"The nuclear accident at Chernobyl happened in 1986, but the area around the plant is still mostly empty today.","t":"車諾比的核子事故發生在1986年，但電廠周圍的地區至今仍大多空無一人。"},{"w":"decommission","p":"v.","d":"to officially stop using a large machine or plant","c":"除役","s":"It will take about twenty years to decommission the old reactor, because every part must be removed and cleaned carefully.","t":"除役這座舊反應爐大約需要二十年，因為每個部分都必須被小心拆除和清理。"},{"w":"spent fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"used nuclear fuel that is still very dangerous","c":"用過核燃料","s":"The spent fuel is kept in deep pools of water for years, because it is still very hot and radioactive.","t":"用過核燃料被存放在深水池中好幾年，因為它仍然非常燙而且具有放射性。"},{"w":"fuel rod","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long metal tube that holds nuclear fuel","c":"燃料棒","s":"Each fuel rod inside the reactor is replaced after a few years, and the old ones must be stored safely.","t":"反應爐內的每一根燃料棒在幾年後就要更換，而舊的必須被安全存放。"},{"w":"coolant","p":"n.","d":"a liquid used to stop a machine from getting too hot","c":"冷卻劑","s":"The reactor must have a steady flow of coolant, because without it the core would become dangerously hot very quickly.","t":"反應爐必須有穩定的冷卻劑流動，因為沒有它，爐心會非常快就變得危險地高溫。"},{"w":"cooling tower","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tall round tower that releases heat from a power plant","c":"冷卻塔","s":"People often think the white cloud above the cooling tower is smoke, but it is actually just water vapour.","t":"人們常以為冷卻塔上方的白雲是煙，但其實那只是水蒸氣。"},{"w":"nuclear-free","p":"adj.","d":"having no nuclear power or weapons","c":"非核的","s":"Some citizens want a nuclear-free homeland, while others think nuclear power is necessary to reduce carbon emissions.","t":"有些市民想要非核家園，而另一些人則認為核能對減少碳排放是必要的。"},{"w":"radioactivity","p":"n.","d":"the harmful energy given off by some materials","c":"放射性；輻射能","s":"Scientists measured the radioactivity in the soil after the accident, and they found that some farms were no longer safe.","t":"科學家在事故後測量土壤中的放射性，他們發現有些農場已經不再安全。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"Mining & Minerals 採礦與礦物","cards":[{"w":"mining","p":"n.","d":"the work of digging minerals out of the ground","c":"採礦","s":"mining is the main industry in this region, so many families depend on it for their income.","t":"採礦是這個地區的主要產業，所以許多家庭仰賴它維持收入。"},{"w":"mine","p":"n.","d":"a deep hole or tunnels where minerals are dug out","c":"礦坑","s":"My great-grandfather worked in a gold mine for thirty years, and he often told stories about the dark tunnels.","t":"我曾祖父在金礦坑工作了三十年，他常常講那些黑暗坑道的故事。"},{"w":"open-pit mine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mine dug as a huge hole from the surface","c":"露天礦","s":"The open-pit mine is so big that you can see it from space, and the trucks inside look like tiny toys.","t":"這座露天礦大到從太空就看得見，裡面的卡車看起來就像小玩具。"},{"w":"strip mining","p":"n.phr.","d":"removing the top layer of land to reach coal","c":"露天剝採","s":"strip mining destroyed the forests on the hills, so the company now has to plant new trees and restore the soil.","t":"露天剝採摧毀了山丘上的森林，所以公司現在必須種新樹並恢復土壤。"},{"w":"deep-sea mining","p":"n.phr.","d":"taking metals from the bottom of the ocean","c":"深海採礦","s":"Scientists warn that deep-sea mining could harm creatures we have not discovered yet, but companies say the metals are needed.","t":"科學家警告深海採礦可能傷害我們尚未發現的生物，但公司表示這些金屬是必需的。"},{"w":"mining town","p":"n.phr.","d":"a town built around a mine","c":"礦業小鎮","s":"Jiufen was once a busy mining town, but now it is famous for its tea houses and beautiful views.","t":"九份曾經是繁忙的礦業小鎮，但現在它以茶館和美麗景色聞名。"},{"w":"ore deposit","p":"n.phr.","d":"a natural collection of rock containing useful metal","c":"礦床","s":"Geologists found a rich ore deposit in the mountains, and a company soon asked for permission to start digging.","t":"地質學家在山中發現了一處豐富的礦床，一家公司很快就申請開挖許可。"},{"w":"rare earth elements","p":"n.phr.","d":"special metals used in phones, magnets and electric cars","c":"稀土元素","s":"Your smartphone contains several rare earth elements, and most of them come from mines in just a few countries.","t":"你的智慧型手機含有好幾種稀土元素，而其中大多數來自少數幾個國家的礦場。"},{"w":"lithium","p":"n.","d":"a light metal used in rechargeable batteries","c":"鋰","s":"Demand for lithium has grown quickly because electric cars need it for their batteries, so its price has gone up.","t":"對鋰的需求快速成長，因為電動車的電池需要它，所以它的價格上漲了。"},{"w":"cobalt","p":"n.","d":"a hard metal used in batteries and blue colours","c":"鈷","s":"Much of the world's cobalt comes from Central Africa, and some mines there have been criticised for using child workers.","t":"世界上大部分的鈷來自中非，而那裡有些礦場因使用童工而遭受批評。"},{"w":"nickel","p":"n.","d":"a silver-coloured metal used in batteries and coins","c":"鎳","s":"Indonesia produces a lot of nickel, and it wants to build battery factories instead of only selling the raw metal.","t":"印尼生產大量的鎳，它想要建造電池工廠，而不只是出售原料金屬。"},{"w":"gold","p":"n.","d":"a valuable yellow metal","c":"黃金","s":"People often buy gold when the economy is uncertain, because they believe its value will stay high.","t":"經濟不確定時人們常購買黃金，因為他們相信它的價值會維持在高點。"},{"w":"silver","p":"n.","d":"a valuable shiny grey metal","c":"銀","s":"silver is used in solar panels as well as jewellery, so the growing solar industry has increased its price.","t":"銀除了用在珠寶，也用在太陽能板上，所以成長中的太陽能產業推升了它的價格。"},{"w":"platinum","p":"n.","d":"a rare and valuable silver-white metal","c":"鉑；白金","s":"Car makers use platinum to clean exhaust gases, and it is also used in hydrogen fuel cells.","t":"汽車製造商使用白金來淨化廢氣，它也被用在氫燃料電池中。"},{"w":"aluminium","p":"n.","d":"a light silver metal used for cans and planes","c":"鋁","s":"Recycling one aluminium can saves enough energy to run a television for three hours, so please do not throw cans away.","t":"回收一個鋁罐所節省的能源足以讓電視運轉三小時，所以請不要把罐子丟掉。"},{"w":"bauxite","p":"n.","d":"the rock from which aluminium is made","c":"鋁土礦","s":"Australia exports huge amounts of bauxite, and factories in other countries turn it into aluminium for cans and cars.","t":"澳洲出口大量的鋁土礦，其他國家的工廠把它製成用於罐子和汽車的鋁。"},{"w":"zinc","p":"n.","d":"a blue-white metal used to protect steel from rust","c":"鋅","s":"The steel roof is covered with a thin layer of zinc, so it does not rust even in the wet coastal weather.","t":"鋼製屋頂覆蓋著一層薄薄的鋅，所以即使在潮濕的海邊氣候中也不會生鏽。"},{"w":"tin","p":"n.","d":"a soft silver metal often used to coat other metals","c":"錫","s":"Electronic parts are joined with a mix that contains tin, so this metal is important for the phone industry.","t":"電子零件是用含有錫的焊料連接的，所以這種金屬對手機產業很重要。"},{"w":"diamond","p":"n.","d":"a very hard, clear and valuable stone","c":"鑽石","s":"Some diamond are mined in war zones, so many buyers now ask for proof that their stones were mined fairly.","t":"有些鑽石是在戰區開採的，所以許多買家現在要求證明他們的寶石是以公平方式開採的。"},{"w":"precious metal","p":"n.phr.","d":"a rare metal of high value, such as gold","c":"貴金屬","s":"Old phones contain small amounts of precious metal, so recycling them can be more profitable than mining new ore.","t":"舊手機含有少量的貴金屬，所以回收它們可能比開採新礦更有利可圖。"},{"w":"prospector","p":"n.","d":"a person who searches for gold or minerals","c":"探礦者","s":"In the 1800s, a lucky prospector could become rich overnight, but most people who searched for gold found nothing.","t":"在十九世紀，一位幸運的探礦者可能一夜致富，但大多數尋找黃金的人一無所獲。"},{"w":"gold rush","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when many people rush to a place to find gold","c":"淘金熱","s":"The California gold rush brought thousands of people to the west, and small villages quickly grew into busy cities.","t":"加州淘金熱吸引了數千人前往西部，小村莊很快發展成繁忙的城市。"},{"w":"excavator","p":"n.","d":"a large machine used for digging","c":"挖土機","s":"A huge excavator was digging up the hillside, so the road was closed and we had to take a longer way home.","t":"一台巨大的挖土機正在挖山坡，所以道路封閉，我們只好繞遠路回家。"},{"w":"tailings","p":"n.","d":"waste rock and mud left after mining","c":"尾礦","s":"The dam holding the mine's tailings broke after heavy rain, and toxic mud flowed into the river and killed the fish.","t":"圍住礦場尾礦的壩在豪雨後潰堤，有毒的泥漿流入河中，毒死了魚。"},{"w":"slag","p":"n.","d":"waste material left after metal is taken from rock","c":"爐渣","s":"The steel factory used to dump its slag near the beach, but now it turns this waste into material for roads.","t":"這家鋼鐵廠過去把爐渣倒在海灘附近，但現在把這種廢料變成鋪路材料。"},{"w":"mineral rights","p":"n.phr.","d":"the legal right to take minerals from a piece of land","c":"礦業權","s":"The farmer owns the land, but a company bought the mineral rights, so it can dig under his fields.","t":"這位農夫擁有這塊地，但一家公司買下了礦業權，所以它可以在他的田地底下開挖。"},{"w":"conflict minerals","p":"n.phr.","d":"minerals mined in war areas that help pay for fighting","c":"衝突礦產","s":"Tech companies promise not to use conflict minerals, because they do not want their products to support violence.","t":"科技公司承諾不使用衝突礦產，因為他們不希望自己的產品支持暴力。"},{"w":"sand mining","p":"n.phr.","d":"taking sand from rivers and beaches for building","c":"採砂","s":"Illegal sand mining has made the river much deeper, so the bridge is now in danger of falling down.","t":"非法採砂讓河道變得深很多，所以那座橋現在有倒塌的危險。"},{"w":"smelter","p":"n.","d":"a factory where metal is taken out of rock by heating","c":"冶煉廠","s":"The copper smelter near the river closed down, so hundreds of workers lost their jobs but the air became cleaner.","t":"河邊的銅冶煉廠關閉了，所以數百名工人失業，但空氣變乾淨了。"},{"w":"scrap metal","p":"n.phr.","d":"old metal that can be melted and used again","c":"廢金屬","s":"My neighbour collects scrap metal from old cars and machines, and he sells it to a recycling factory every week.","t":"我鄰居從舊車和機器收集廢金屬，每週把它賣給回收工廠。"},{"w":"seismic survey","p":"n.phr.","d":"a study that uses sound waves to look under the ground","c":"震測調查","s":"The company carried out a seismic survey in the bay, but environmental groups said the loud noise could hurt whales.","t":"這家公司在海灣進行了震測調查，但環保團體說巨大的噪音可能傷害鯨魚。"},{"w":"iron","p":"n.","d":"a strong grey metal used to make steel","c":"鐵","s":"iron is mixed with a little carbon to make steel, so it is one of the most important metals in the world.","t":"鐵加入少量的碳就能製成鋼，所以它是世界上最重要的金屬之一。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"Natural Resources & Scarcity 天然資源與短缺","cards":[{"w":"natural resources","p":"n.phr.","d":"things from nature that people use, like water and oil","c":"天然資源","s":"Taiwan has few natural resources of its own, so it must import most of its oil, gas and coal.","t":"台灣本身的天然資源很少，所以必須進口大部分的石油、天然氣和煤。"},{"w":"resource depletion","p":"n.phr.","d":"using up natural resources faster than they return","c":"資源耗竭","s":"resource depletion is a serious problem for future generations, because many materials cannot be replaced once they are gone.","t":"資源耗竭對未來世代是個嚴重問題，因為許多材料一旦用完就無法替代。"},{"w":"water supply","p":"n.phr.","d":"the water provided to an area for people to use","c":"供水","s":"The water supply was cut for two days during the drought, so families had to collect water from trucks.","t":"乾旱期間供水中斷了兩天，所以家家戶戶只好向水車取水。"},{"w":"water shortage","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation when there is not enough water","c":"缺水","s":"Chip factories use a lot of water, so a water shortage in spring can be a serious problem for the whole economy.","t":"晶片工廠用水量很大，所以春季缺水可能成為整個經濟的嚴重問題。"},{"w":"borehole","p":"n.","d":"a deep narrow hole dug to find water or oil","c":"鑽孔；水井","s":"The charity dug a new borehole in the village, so children no longer have to walk hours every day to fetch water.","t":"慈善機構在村子裡鑿了一口新的水井，所以孩子們不再需要每天走好幾個小時去取水。"},{"w":"well","p":"n.","d":"a hole dug in the ground to get water","c":"井","s":"The old well in the temple yard dried up during the drought, but the villagers hope it will fill again after the rains.","t":"寺廟院子裡的老井在乾旱期間乾涸了，但村民希望下雨後它會再度有水。"},{"w":"non-renewable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be replaced once it has been used","c":"不可再生的","s":"Coal and oil are non-renewable resources, so we will eventually run out of them if we keep burning them.","t":"煤和石油是不可再生資源，所以如果我們持續燃燒它們，終有一天會用光。"},{"w":"finite resource","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that exists only in a limited amount","c":"有限資源","s":"Clean water is a finite resource in many places, so people should not waste it while washing cars or watering lawns.","t":"在許多地方乾淨的水是有限資源，所以人們在洗車或澆草坪時不應浪費。"},{"w":"resource-rich","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of natural resources","c":"資源豐富的","s":"Some resource-rich countries are still poor, because the money from oil and minerals does not reach ordinary people.","t":"有些資源豐富的國家仍然貧窮，因為來自石油和礦產的錢沒有流到一般百姓手中。"},{"w":"resource curse","p":"n.phr.","d":"when rich natural resources lead to poor development","c":"資源詛咒","s":"Economists use the term resource curse to describe countries where oil money causes corruption and slows growth.","t":"經濟學家用資源詛咒這個詞來描述石油收入導致貪腐、拖慢成長的國家。"},{"w":"overextraction","p":"n.","d":"taking too much of a resource from the ground","c":"過度抽取","s":"overextraction of groundwater has made the land sink along the coast, so some homes now flood at every high tide.","t":"地下水的過度抽取使沿海地層下陷，所以有些房屋現在每逢漲潮就淹水。"},{"w":"water rights","p":"n.phr.","d":"the legal right to use water from a river or lake","c":"水權","s":"Farmers and factories are arguing over water rights, because there is not enough river water for both groups this year.","t":"農民和工廠正為水權爭執，因為今年的河水不夠兩方使用。"},{"w":"rainwater harvesting","p":"n.phr.","d":"collecting rain so it can be used later","c":"雨水回收","s":"Our school uses rainwater harvesting to water the gardens, so we save tap water and reduce our water bill.","t":"我們學校利用雨水回收來澆灌花園，所以既節省自來水，也降低了水費。"},{"w":"recycling","p":"n.","d":"treating used things so they can be used again","c":"回收","s":"recycling old phones keeps valuable metals in use, and it also stops toxic materials from ending up in landfill.","t":"回收舊手機能讓珍貴金屬持續被利用，也能防止有毒物質最後進入掩埋場。"},{"w":"e-waste","p":"n.","d":"thrown-away electronic devices like phones and computers","c":"電子廢棄物","s":"Piles of e-waste are shipped to poor countries, where workers burn cables to get the copper and breathe in toxic smoke.","t":"成堆的電子廢棄物被運到貧窮國家，那裡的工人燒電線取銅，吸入有毒煙霧。"},{"w":"circular economy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a system where products are reused and recycled, not thrown away","c":"循環經濟","s":"In a circular economy, old products are repaired or recycled, so fewer new raw materials need to be dug from the ground.","t":"在循環經濟中，舊產品會被修理或回收，所以需要從地下挖掘的新原料就比較少。"},{"w":"resource efficiency","p":"n.phr.","d":"using fewer materials to make the same product","c":"資源效率","s":"The factory improved its resource efficiency by reusing water and metal scraps, and it saved a lot of money as well.","t":"這家工廠透過再利用水和金屬碎料提高了資源效率，也省下了很多錢。"},{"w":"energy security","p":"n.phr.","d":"having a reliable supply of energy at a fair price","c":"能源安全","s":"Taiwan imports almost all its fuel, so energy security is a major concern if shipping routes are ever blocked.","t":"台灣幾乎所有燃料都靠進口，所以若航道遭封鎖，能源安全就是一大隱憂。"},{"w":"energy crisis","p":"n.phr.","d":"a serious shortage of energy and very high prices","c":"能源危機","s":"During the energy crisis in 2022, gas prices in Europe rose so much that some factories had to close.","t":"在2022年的能源危機期間，歐洲天然氣價格漲得太多，以致有些工廠不得不關閉。"},{"w":"energy poverty","p":"n.phr.","d":"not being able to afford enough energy at home","c":"能源貧窮","s":"Many elderly people live in energy poverty, so they cannot afford to heat their homes properly in winter.","t":"許多長者處於能源貧窮，所以冬天他們無法負擔讓家裡足夠溫暖的暖氣費用。"},{"w":"energy demand","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of energy that people need","c":"能源需求","s":"energy demand keeps rising because of new data centres, so power companies must build more plants quickly.","t":"能源需求因為新的資料中心而持續上升，所以電力公司必須迅速興建更多電廠。"},{"w":"oil crisis","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when oil becomes very scarce and expensive","c":"石油危機","s":"During the 1973 oil crisis, petrol was so short that people waited in long queues at every station.","t":"在1973年的石油危機期間，汽油短缺到人們在每個加油站都大排長龍。"},{"w":"fuel shortage","p":"n.phr.","d":"a situation when there is not enough fuel","c":"燃料短缺","s":"A fuel shortage hit the country after the port was closed, so buses ran less often and many flights were cancelled.","t":"港口關閉後，這個國家發生燃料短缺，所以公車班次減少，許多航班被取消。"},{"w":"oil-rich","p":"adj.","d":"having large amounts of oil","c":"石油蘊藏豐富的","s":"Many oil-rich countries are now investing in solar power, because they know oil will not last forever.","t":"許多石油蘊藏豐富的國家現在投資太陽能，因為他們知道石油不會永遠存在。"},{"w":"energy independence","p":"n.phr.","d":"producing enough energy without relying on other countries","c":"能源自主","s":"The president promised energy independence within ten years, but experts doubted that the goal was realistic.","t":"總統承諾十年內達成能源自主，但專家懷疑這個目標是否切合實際。"},{"w":"stranded asset","p":"n.phr.","d":"something valuable that loses its value early, like an unused coal plant","c":"擱淺資產","s":"Investors fear the new coal plant will become a stranded asset, because clean energy is getting cheaper every year.","t":"投資人擔心這座新燃煤電廠會變成擱淺資產，因為乾淨能源每年都變得更便宜。"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"Saving Energy at Home & on the Road 居家與交通節能","cards":[{"w":"energy bill","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount you pay for gas and electricity","c":"能源帳單；電費","s":"Our energy bill was very high in August, so we decided to use fans more often instead of the air conditioner.","t":"我們八月的電費非常高，所以我們決定多用電風扇而不是冷氣。"},{"w":"energy-saving","p":"adj.","d":"using less energy than usual","c":"節能的","s":"We replaced all our old light bulbs with energy-saving ones, and our electricity bill dropped noticeably the next month.","t":"我們把所有舊燈泡都換成節能燈泡，隔月的電費明顯降低。"},{"w":"switch off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to turn off a machine or light","c":"關掉","s":"Please switch off the projector after class, because leaving it on all night wastes electricity and shortens its life.","t":"下課後請關掉投影機，因為整夜開著會浪費電，也會縮短它的壽命。"},{"w":"unplug","p":"v.","d":"to take a plug out of a socket","c":"拔掉插頭","s":"Before we went on holiday, my mum told us to unplug the TV and computer, so they would not use power while we were away.","t":"我們去度假之前，媽媽要我們拔掉電視和電腦的插頭，這樣我們不在家時它們就不會耗電。"},{"w":"standby mode","p":"n.phr.","d":"when a machine is off but still uses a little power","c":"待機模式","s":"Many TVs stay in standby mode all night, and together they waste a surprising amount of electricity every year.","t":"許多電視整夜維持在待機模式，加總起來每年浪費的電量驚人。"},{"w":"energy label","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sticker showing how much energy a machine uses","c":"能源標章","s":"Check the energy label before buying a fridge, because a more efficient model will save you money for many years.","t":"買冰箱前要先看能源標章，因為較節能的機型能讓你省錢很多年。"},{"w":"energy efficiency","p":"n.phr.","d":"using less energy to do the same job","c":"能源效率","s":"Improving the energy efficiency of old buildings is one of the cheapest ways to reduce pollution, but many owners ignore it.","t":"提升舊建築的能源效率是減少污染最便宜的方法之一，但許多屋主卻忽略它。"},{"w":"energy consumption","p":"n.phr.","d":"the amount of energy used","c":"能源消耗；耗能","s":"Data centres have greatly increased the country's energy consumption, so the government is asking them to use more renewable power.","t":"資料中心大幅增加了國家的能源消耗，所以政府要求它們使用更多再生能源。"},{"w":"central heating","p":"n.phr.","d":"a system that heats a whole building from one place","c":"中央暖氣","s":"Most houses in Britain have central heating, so the rooms stay warm even when it is snowing outside.","t":"英國大多數房子都有中央暖氣，所以即使外面下雪，房間仍保持溫暖。"},{"w":"radiator","p":"n.","d":"a metal heater on a wall, filled with hot water","c":"暖氣片","s":"I put my wet gloves on the radiator to dry, and they were warm and ready by the time I left for school.","t":"我把濕手套放在暖氣片上烘乾，到我出門上學時它們已經溫暖又乾了。"},{"w":"air conditioner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that makes a room cool","c":"冷氣機","s":"Setting the air conditioner to 26 degrees instead of 22 saves a lot of energy, and the room still feels comfortable.","t":"把冷氣機設定在26度而不是22度能省下很多能源，房間仍然感覺舒適。"},{"w":"electric fan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine with blades that moves air to cool you","c":"電風扇","s":"An electric fan uses much less power than air conditioning, so we use it on days that are warm but not too hot.","t":"電風扇比冷氣省電得多，所以在溫暖但不太熱的日子我們就用它。"},{"w":"dehumidifier","p":"n.","d":"a machine that removes water from the air","c":"除濕機","s":"Our flat gets very damp in spring, so we run a dehumidifier every day to stop our clothes from smelling bad.","t":"我們的公寓在春天非常潮濕，所以我們每天開除濕機，避免衣服產生異味。"},{"w":"space heater","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small portable machine that heats one room","c":"電暖器","s":"My grandmother uses a space heater in her bedroom, but we remind her to keep it away from the curtains.","t":"奶奶在臥室使用電暖器，但我們提醒她要讓它遠離窗簾。"},{"w":"draught","p":"n.","d":"cold air coming into a room through a gap","c":"穿堂風；冷風","s":"There is a cold draught coming under the front door, so we put a long cushion there to keep the heat inside.","t":"有一股冷風從前門底下吹進來，所以我們在那裡放了一個長墊子把熱氣留在屋內。"},{"w":"draught-proof","p":"v.","d":"to block gaps so cold air cannot come in","c":"防風密封","s":"We decided to draught-proof our old windows before winter, and the house now feels much warmer without extra heating.","t":"我們決定在冬天前為舊窗戶做防風密封，現在不用額外開暖氣房子就感覺溫暖許多。"},{"w":"loft insulation","p":"n.phr.","d":"material in the roof space that keeps heat in","c":"閣樓隔熱層","s":"Adding loft insulation is cheap and quick, but it can cut a family's heating costs by a large amount each year.","t":"加裝閣樓隔熱層既便宜又快速，卻能每年大幅降低一個家庭的暖氣費用。"},{"w":"energy audit","p":"n.phr.","d":"a check of how a building uses and wastes energy","c":"能源稽核","s":"An expert did an energy audit of our school, and she found that old lights and computers were wasting a lot of power.","t":"一位專家為我們學校做了能源稽核，她發現舊燈具和電腦浪費了大量電力。"},{"w":"eco mode","p":"n.phr.","d":"a setting that makes a machine use less energy","c":"節能模式","s":"I always use eco mode on the washing machine, because it uses less water and power even though it takes longer.","t":"我洗衣服總是使用節能模式，因為雖然花比較久，但用水和用電都比較少。"},{"w":"hybrid car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a car with both a petrol engine and an electric motor","c":"油電混合車","s":"My uncle bought a hybrid car last year, and he is happy because he now visits the petrol station much less often.","t":"我叔叔去年買了一輛油電混合車，他很開心，因為現在他去加油站的次數少很多。"},{"w":"electric car","p":"n.phr.","d":"a car that runs only on electricity from batteries","c":"電動車","s":"electric car are quiet and produce no exhaust, but some drivers worry that the batteries will run out on long trips.","t":"電動車安靜且不排放廢氣，但有些駕駛擔心長途旅行時電池會沒電。"},{"w":"charging station","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where electric cars can be charged","c":"充電站","s":"There are more charging station in shopping centres now, so drivers can charge their cars while they buy groceries.","t":"現在購物中心有更多充電站，所以駕駛人可以一邊買菜一邊替車子充電。"},{"w":"power bank","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small portable battery for charging phones","c":"行動電源","s":"I always carry a power bank on school trips, because my phone battery runs out quickly when I take lots of photos.","t":"我校外教學時總會帶著行動電源，因為拍很多照片時手機電量很快就用完。"},{"w":"fuel-efficient","p":"adj.","d":"using only a small amount of fuel","c":"省油的","s":"My parents chose a fuel-efficient car because petrol prices keep rising, and they drive to work every day.","t":"我父母選了一輛省油的車，因為油價不斷上漲，而他們每天開車上班。"},{"w":"gas guzzler","p":"n.phr.","d":"a big car that uses a lot of fuel","c":"耗油車","s":"My neighbour finally sold his old gas guzzler, because filling its huge tank every week was costing him too much money.","t":"我鄰居終於賣掉了他那輛老耗油車，因為每週加滿它的大油箱讓他花太多錢。"},{"w":"smart plug","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plug you can control with your phone","c":"智慧插座","s":"I connected the heater to a smart plug, so I can turn it on from my phone before I get home.","t":"我把暖氣機接上智慧插座，所以我可以在到家前用手機打開它。"},{"w":"smart thermostat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that controls heating and learns your habits","c":"智慧溫控器","s":"Our smart thermostat lowers the heating when nobody is home, and it warms the house again just before we return.","t":"我們的智慧溫控器在沒人在家時會調低暖氣，並在我們回來之前讓房子再度變暖。"},{"w":"heat loss","p":"n.phr.","d":"heat escaping from a building","c":"熱能流失","s":"Most heat loss in old houses happens through the roof and windows, so these are the first places to improve.","t":"老房子大部分的熱能流失發生在屋頂和窗戶，所以這些是最先需要改善的地方。"},{"w":"motion sensor","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that turns on when it notices movement","c":"動作感應器","s":"The lights in our school toilets have a motion sensor, so they turn off automatically when nobody is inside.","t":"我們學校廁所的燈裝有動作感應器，所以沒人在裡面時會自動關燈。"},{"w":"kettle","p":"n.","d":"a container for boiling water","c":"熱水壺","s":"Only boil as much water as you need in the kettle, because heating extra water wastes both time and electricity.","t":"用熱水壺只煮你需要的水量，因為加熱多餘的水既浪費時間也浪費電。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 1 (abolition – curtailment)","cards":[{"w":"abolition","p":"n.","d":"the official ending of a law or system","c":"廢除","s":"The abolition of fuel subsidies made petrol more expensive, so taxi drivers held a protest outside the government building.","t":"燃料補貼的廢除讓汽油變貴，所以計程車司機在政府大樓外抗議。"},{"w":"absence","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being there","c":"缺乏；不在","s":"In the absence of strong wind, the turbines stood still all week, so the grid had to use more gas power.","t":"在缺乏強風的情況下，風機整週都靜止不動，所以電網必須使用更多燃氣發電。"},{"w":"acceptability","p":"n.","d":"how far something is accepted by people","c":"可接受度","s":"Public acceptability is important for new power plants, because projects often fail when local residents strongly oppose them.","t":"民眾的可接受度對新電廠很重要，因為當地居民強烈反對時，計畫常常會失敗。"},{"w":"activism","p":"n.","d":"action taken to bring about social or political change","c":"社會運動；行動主義","s":"Student activism helped stop the coal plant, because young people organised marches and wrote thousands of letters to officials.","t":"學生的社會運動幫助阻止了燃煤電廠，因為年輕人組織遊行並寫了數千封信給官員。"},{"w":"advisory","p":"adj.","d":"giving advice","c":"顧問的；諮詢的","s":"The minister set up an advisory group of scientists, and it will suggest ways to cut energy use in public buildings.","t":"部長成立了一個由科學家組成的諮詢小組，它將建議減少公共建築用電的方法。"},{"w":"amplification","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something larger or stronger","c":"擴大；放大","s":"Social media led to the amplification of fears about nuclear power, so many people became anxious even without new evidence.","t":"社群媒體造成對核能恐懼的擴大，所以即使沒有新證據，很多人仍變得焦慮。"},{"w":"analogue","p":"adj.","d":"using older, non-digital technology","c":"類比式的","s":"Our building still has an analogue electricity meter, so a worker has to visit every month to read the numbers.","t":"我們大樓仍使用類比式電表，所以每個月都要有工作人員來抄錶。"},{"w":"anticipatory","p":"adj.","d":"done before something is expected to happen","c":"預先的；預期性的","s":"The city took anticipatory action before the summer, so extra power was ready when the heatwave arrived.","t":"市政府在夏天前採取了預先行動，所以熱浪來襲時已準備好額外電力。"},{"w":"asymmetry","p":"n.","d":"a lack of balance between two sides","c":"不對稱","s":"There is an asymmetry in information between energy companies and customers, so many people do not understand their own bills.","t":"能源公司和顧客之間存在資訊不對稱，所以許多人看不懂自己的帳單。"},{"w":"bearable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be accepted or dealt with","c":"可忍受的","s":"The fan made the hot classroom more bearable, but students still found it difficult to concentrate in the afternoon.","t":"電風扇讓炎熱的教室變得比較可以忍受，但學生下午仍覺得很難專心。"},{"w":"boundless","p":"adj.","d":"without limits","c":"無限的","s":"The sun provides almost boundless energy, but we still need better ways to store it for the night.","t":"太陽提供幾乎無限的能源，但我們仍需要更好的方法把它儲存到夜晚使用。"},{"w":"centralised","p":"adj.","d":"controlled from one main place","c":"集中的","s":"The old system was highly centralised, so one problem at a large power plant could cause blackouts across the whole country.","t":"舊系統高度集中，所以大型電廠的一個問題就可能造成全國大停電。"},{"w":"conductive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing electricity or heat to pass through","c":"導電的；傳導的","s":"Copper is very conductive, so it is used for most electrical wires, but it is becoming more expensive.","t":"銅非常導電，所以大多數電線都使用它，但它正變得越來越貴。"},{"w":"conductivity","p":"n.","d":"how easily electricity or heat moves through a material","c":"導電性；傳導率","s":"Silver has the highest conductivity of all metals, but it is too expensive to use for ordinary household wiring.","t":"銀在所有金屬中導電性最高，但它太貴了，無法用於一般家用電線。"},{"w":"consequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening as a result of something","c":"隨之而來的","s":"The drought and the consequent fall in river levels meant that the hydroelectric dams produced much less power.","t":"乾旱和隨之而來的河川水位下降，意味著水力發電水壩的發電量少了很多。"},{"w":"consumable","p":"n.","d":"a product that is used up and must be replaced","c":"消耗品","s":"Printer ink and paper are consumable in the office, so the school is trying to reduce how much it buys.","t":"印表機墨水和紙張是辦公室的消耗品，所以學校正試著減少購買量。"},{"w":"continual","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again","c":"不斷的；頻繁的","s":"The village suffered from continual power cuts last summer, so many families bought small generators for their homes.","t":"這個村莊去年夏天飽受頻繁的停電之苦，所以許多家庭替家裡買了小型發電機。"},{"w":"contributory","p":"adj.","d":"helping to cause something","c":"促成的","s":"Old wiring was a contributory factor in the fire, but the main cause was a heater left on overnight.","t":"老舊電線是這場火災的促成因素之一，但主要原因是暖氣機整夜開著。"},{"w":"controversially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes public disagreement","c":"具爭議地","s":"The council controversially approved a new gas plant, and many residents said they had not been asked for their opinions.","t":"市議會具爭議地核准了一座新燃氣電廠，許多居民說他們沒被徵詢意見。"},{"w":"conventionally","p":"adv.","d":"in the usual, traditional way","c":"傳統上；按慣例","s":"Electricity was conventionally produced by burning coal, but today many countries are using more solar and wind power.","t":"電力傳統上是靠燃燒煤炭生產的，但如今許多國家使用更多太陽能和風力發電。"},{"w":"convertible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed into another form","c":"可轉換的","s":"Heat from the factory is convertible into electricity, so the company now produces part of its own power.","t":"工廠的熱能可轉換成電力，所以公司現在可以自行生產部分電力。"},{"w":"correlated","p":"adj.","d":"closely connected, so one changes with the other","c":"相關的","s":"Energy use is closely correlated with temperature, so electricity demand rises sharply whenever a heatwave hits the city.","t":"能源使用和氣溫密切相關，所以每當熱浪侵襲城市，電力需求就會急劇上升。"},{"w":"cost-effectiveness","p":"n.","d":"how much benefit you get for the money spent","c":"成本效益","s":"The study compared the cost-effectiveness of solar panels and insulation, and it found that insulation saved money faster.","t":"這項研究比較了太陽能板和隔熱材料的成本效益，發現隔熱材料省錢更快。"},{"w":"countermeasure","p":"n.","d":"an action taken to reduce a danger or problem","c":"對策","s":"Energy prices kept rising, so the government introduced several countermeasure, such as cash support for poor families.","t":"能源價格持續上漲，所以政府推出了幾項對策，例如為貧困家庭提供現金補助。"},{"w":"curtailment","p":"n.","d":"the act of reducing or limiting something","c":"削減；限制","s":"On very sunny days there is curtailment of solar power, because the grid cannot use all the electricity being produced.","t":"在陽光非常充足的日子會削減太陽能發電，因為電網無法使用所有產生的電力。"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 2 (decentralised – extractive)","cards":[{"w":"decentralised","p":"adj.","d":"spread out instead of controlled from one place","c":"分散式的","s":"A decentralised energy system uses many small power sources, so one failure does not shut down the whole network.","t":"分散式能源系統使用許多小型電源，所以單一故障不會讓整個電網停擺。"},{"w":"declining","p":"adj.","d":"becoming less or smaller","c":"逐漸減少的","s":"The town's declining coal industry has left many shops empty, but a new battery factory may bring jobs back.","t":"鎮上日漸衰退的煤礦產業讓許多商店空置，但一座新電池工廠可能把工作帶回來。"},{"w":"dedicated","p":"adj.","d":"used only for one particular purpose","c":"專用的","s":"The car park has ten dedicated spaces for electric cars, and each one has its own charging point.","t":"停車場有十個電動車專用車位，每一個都有自己的充電樁。"},{"w":"degradation","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming worse in quality","c":"退化；劣化","s":"Battery degradation means that phones hold less charge after a few years, so many people replace them too early.","t":"電池劣化意味著手機幾年後蓄電量變少，所以許多人太早換掉手機。"},{"w":"deployment","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting something into use","c":"部署；推廣使用","s":"The rapid deployment of solar panels has lowered their price, so more families can now afford them.","t":"太陽能板的快速推廣降低了價格，所以現在更多家庭負擔得起。"},{"w":"deregulate","p":"v.","d":"to remove government rules from an industry","c":"解除管制","s":"The government decided to deregulate the electricity market, so new companies can now compete with the old state supplier.","t":"政府決定對電力市場解除管制，所以新公司現在可以和老牌國營供應商競爭。"},{"w":"desirability","p":"n.","d":"how much something is wanted or seen as good","c":"可取性；吸引力","s":"The desirability of nuclear power is still debated, because it is low-carbon but produces dangerous waste.","t":"核能的可取性仍有爭議，因為它低碳卻產生危險廢料。"},{"w":"deteriorating","p":"adj.","d":"becoming worse","c":"惡化中的","s":"The deteriorating condition of the old pipes caused several gas leaks, so the city decided to replace them all.","t":"舊管線日益惡化的狀況造成好幾起瓦斯外洩，所以市政府決定全部更換。"},{"w":"devastation","p":"n.","d":"very great damage","c":"嚴重破壞","s":"The oil spill caused terrible devastation along the coast, and it took years for the fishing industry to recover.","t":"漏油事件沿著海岸造成了可怕的嚴重破壞，漁業花了好幾年才復原。"},{"w":"diminution","p":"n.","d":"a reduction in size or importance","c":"減少；縮小","s":"There has been a steady diminution in coal's share of power, while solar and wind have grown each year.","t":"煤炭在發電中的占比穩定減少，而太陽能和風力每年都在成長。"},{"w":"disadvantage","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a situation less good","c":"缺點","s":"One disadvantage of wind power is the noise, so some people do not want turbines built near their homes.","t":"風力發電的一個缺點是噪音，所以有些人不希望風機蓋在家附近。"},{"w":"discontinuation","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something","c":"停止；中止","s":"The discontinuation of the bus service forced many villagers to drive, so fuel use in the area actually went up.","t":"公車服務的停駛迫使許多村民開車，所以這個地區的燃料使用量反而增加了。"},{"w":"dissipation","p":"n.","d":"the gradual loss of energy, often as heat","c":"散失；消散","s":"Some power is always lost through heat dissipation in long cables, so engineers use high voltages to reduce waste.","t":"長距離電纜總會因熱能散失而損失一些電力，所以工程師使用高壓來減少浪費。"},{"w":"distributional","p":"adj.","d":"related to how something is shared among people","c":"分配的","s":"The carbon tax has distributional effects, because poorer families spend a larger part of their income on energy.","t":"碳稅有分配效應，因為較貧窮的家庭在能源上花費的收入比例較高。"},{"w":"downward","p":"adj.","d":"moving towards a lower level","c":"向下的","s":"Solar prices have followed a downward trend for twenty years, so the technology is now cheaper than coal in many places.","t":"太陽能價格二十年來呈下降趨勢，所以這項技術如今在許多地方比煤還便宜。"},{"w":"dwindling","p":"adj.","d":"becoming gradually smaller in amount","c":"日漸減少的","s":"The country's dwindling gas supplies have pushed it to import more, so its energy bills have risen sharply.","t":"這個國家日漸減少的天然氣供應迫使它進口更多，所以能源費用急劇上升。"},{"w":"electrifying","p":"adj.","d":"extremely exciting","c":"令人振奮的；激動人心的","s":"The scientist gave an electrifying speech about clean energy, and many students decided to study engineering afterwards.","t":"那位科學家發表了一場關於乾淨能源激動人心的演講，之後許多學生決定念工程。"},{"w":"encompassing","p":"adj.","d":"including many different things","c":"涵蓋廣泛的","s":"The new energy plan is broad and encompassing, because it covers transport, housing and industry instead of just power stations.","t":"新的能源計畫範圍廣且涵蓋全面，因為它涵蓋交通、住宅和工業，而不只是發電廠。"},{"w":"endless","p":"adj.","d":"seeming to have no end","c":"無止境的","s":"We are not living with an endless supply of oil, so we must start using cleaner sources soon.","t":"我們並不是擁有無止境的石油供應，所以我們必須盡快開始使用更乾淨的能源。"},{"w":"energetic","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of energy and enthusiasm","c":"精力充沛的","s":"Our energetic science teacher started a recycling club, and now students collect hundreds of cans every week.","t":"我們精力充沛的自然老師創立了回收社團，現在學生每週收集數百個罐子。"},{"w":"estimation","p":"n.","d":"a judgement of an amount without exact measuring","c":"估計","s":"By my estimation, our family could save about two thousand dollars a year if we used less air conditioning.","t":"根據我的估計，如果我們少開冷氣，我們家一年大約能省下兩千元。"},{"w":"exhaustible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be completely used up","c":"可耗盡的","s":"Oil is an exhaustible resource, so countries that depend on it must plan for the day it runs out.","t":"石油是可耗盡的資源，所以依賴它的國家必須為它用完的那天做準備。"},{"w":"expandable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be made larger","c":"可擴充的","s":"The battery system is expandable, so the school can add more units later when it installs more solar panels.","t":"這套電池系統是可擴充的，所以學校日後加裝更多太陽能板時可以增加更多單元。"},{"w":"exploitable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used for profit","c":"可開採的；可利用的","s":"Only a small part of the gas under the sea is exploitable, because the rest is too deep or too costly to reach.","t":"海底的天然氣只有一小部分是可開採的，因為其餘的太深或成本太高而難以取得。"},{"w":"extractive","p":"adj.","d":"related to taking resources out of the ground","c":"採掘的","s":"extractive industries like mining create jobs, but they often leave serious damage to the land and water.","t":"像採礦這樣的採掘產業創造了工作，但它們常對土地和水源留下嚴重破壞。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 3 (fallback – multiplier)","cards":[{"w":"fallback","p":"n.","d":"a plan or option kept for when others fail","c":"備案","s":"The hospital uses diesel generators as a fallback, so it can keep operating even during a long power cut.","t":"醫院以柴油發電機作為備案，所以即使長時間停電也能持續運作。"},{"w":"fluctuating","p":"adj.","d":"rising and falling often","c":"波動的","s":"fluctuating oil prices make it hard for airlines to plan, so they often buy fuel months in advance.","t":"波動的油價讓航空公司難以規劃，所以他們常提前數月購買燃料。"},{"w":"forecasting","p":"n.","d":"predicting what will happen in the future","c":"預測","s":"Better weather forecasting helps grid operators prepare, because they know when solar and wind power will be low.","t":"更好的天氣預測幫助電網營運者做準備，因為他們知道太陽能和風力何時會偏低。"},{"w":"foreseeable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be predicted","c":"可預見的","s":"Coal will still be used in the foreseeable future, but its share of electricity is expected to fall steadily.","t":"在可預見的未來煤炭仍會被使用，但它在電力中的占比預計將穩定下降。"},{"w":"fragmentary","p":"adj.","d":"incomplete and in small parts","c":"零碎的","s":"The data on energy use in villages is fragmentary, so researchers had to visit homes to collect better information.","t":"村莊能源使用的資料很零碎，所以研究人員必須親自家訪以收集更好的資訊。"},{"w":"fundamentals","p":"n.","d":"the basic and most important parts of something","c":"基本原理；基礎","s":"Our teacher explained the fundamentals of electricity first, and then we built simple circuits with batteries and bulbs.","t":"老師先解釋了電的基本原理，然後我們用電池和燈泡做了簡單的電路。"},{"w":"geopolitics","p":"n.","d":"how geography affects international politics","c":"地緣政治","s":"Energy and geopolitics are closely linked, because countries that control oil and gas can put pressure on their neighbours.","t":"能源和地緣政治緊密相關，因為控制石油和天然氣的國家可以對鄰國施壓。"},{"w":"globalised","p":"adj.","d":"connected across the whole world","c":"全球化的","s":"In a globalised economy, a war far away can raise petrol prices at home, so no country is completely safe.","t":"在全球化的經濟中，遠方的戰爭也能讓國內油價上漲，所以沒有國家是完全安全的。"},{"w":"immediacy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being urgent and happening now","c":"迫切性；即時性","s":"The immediacy of the energy crisis forced leaders to act quickly, but some of their decisions were not well planned.","t":"能源危機的迫切性迫使領導人迅速行動，但他們有些決定並未經過周詳規劃。"},{"w":"inaction","p":"n.","d":"failure to do anything","c":"不作為","s":"Many young people are angry about government inaction on energy, because they will live with the results the longest.","t":"許多年輕人對政府在能源議題上的不作為感到憤怒，因為他們將承受後果最久。"},{"w":"incapable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to do something","c":"無法的；沒有能力的","s":"The old grid is incapable of handling so much solar power, so engineers must upgrade it soon.","t":"舊電網無法處理這麼多太陽能電力，所以工程師必須盡快升級它。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"freedom from control or help by others","c":"獨立；自主","s":"Our village wants greater independence from the national grid, so we are building a small solar and battery system.","t":"我們村莊希望更獨立於國家電網，所以我們正在建造小型太陽能與電池系統。"},{"w":"industrialise","p":"v.","d":"to develop industries in a country or area","c":"工業化","s":"As poorer countries industrialise, their energy use rises quickly, so they need affordable and clean power sources.","t":"隨著較貧窮的國家工業化，它們的能源使用量迅速上升，所以需要便宜又乾淨的電力來源。"},{"w":"inelastic","p":"adj.","d":"not changing much when price changes","c":"缺乏彈性的","s":"Demand for electricity is quite inelastic, because people still need lights and fridges even when prices go up.","t":"電力需求相當缺乏彈性，因為即使價格上漲，人們仍需要電燈和冰箱。"},{"w":"infeasible","p":"adj.","d":"not possible to do in practice","c":"不可行的","s":"Building a dam in the earthquake zone was judged infeasible, so the engineers chose a different valley instead.","t":"在地震帶興建水壩被判定為不可行，所以工程師改選了另一個山谷。"},{"w":"inflexible","p":"adj.","d":"unable to change easily","c":"缺乏彈性的；僵化的","s":"Nuclear plants are fairly inflexible, because they cannot quickly increase or decrease their power to match demand.","t":"核電廠相當缺乏彈性，因為它們無法迅速增減發電量來配合需求。"},{"w":"insecurity","p":"n.","d":"a lack of safety or certainty","c":"不安全；不穩定","s":"Energy insecurity grew when the shipping route was blocked, so the government asked people to save electricity.","t":"航道被封鎖時能源不安全感升高，所以政府呼籲民眾節約用電。"},{"w":"insufficiency","p":"n.","d":"a lack of enough of something","c":"不足","s":"An insufficiency of rain this spring meant the reservoirs were low, so water had to be rationed in some cities.","t":"今年春天雨量不足導致水庫水位偏低，所以一些城市必須限水。"},{"w":"interconnection","p":"n.","d":"a link between two or more things","c":"互聯；相互連接","s":"The interconnection between the two countries' grids allows them to share power, so a shortage in one can be covered by the other.","t":"兩國電網之間的互聯讓它們能共享電力，所以一方短缺時可由另一方補足。"},{"w":"long-range","p":"adj.","d":"covering a long distance or period","c":"長程的；長期的","s":"long-range electric buses can now travel 400 kilometres on one charge, so they are suitable for trips between cities.","t":"長程電動巴士現在充一次電可以行駛四百公里，所以適合城市間的行程。"},{"w":"maximisation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something as large as possible","c":"最大化","s":"Profit maximisation was the company's main goal, so it ignored complaints about pollution from its factory.","t":"利潤最大化是這家公司的主要目標，所以它忽視了關於工廠污染的投訴。"},{"w":"minimisation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something as small as possible","c":"最小化","s":"Waste minimisation is part of our school policy, so we use refillable bottles and print on both sides of paper.","t":"廢棄物最小化是我們學校政策的一部分，所以我們使用可重複裝填的水壺，並且雙面列印。"},{"w":"modernisation","p":"n.","d":"the process of making something more up to date","c":"現代化","s":"The modernisation of the old power station cost billions, but it now produces more electricity with less pollution.","t":"舊電廠的現代化耗資數十億，但它現在以更少污染產生更多電力。"},{"w":"monopolise","p":"v.","d":"to have complete control of something","c":"壟斷","s":"One company used to monopolise the electricity market, so customers had no choice and prices stayed high.","t":"過去一家公司壟斷了電力市場，所以顧客別無選擇，價格一直居高不下。"},{"w":"multiplier","p":"n.","d":"something that increases the effect of something else","c":"乘數；倍增因素","s":"Cheap energy acts as a multiplier for economic growth, because factories can produce more goods at lower cost.","t":"廉價能源是經濟成長的倍增因素，因為工廠能以較低成本生產更多商品。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 4 (nationalise – uncertain)","cards":[{"w":"nationalise","p":"v.","d":"to bring a private company under government control","c":"收歸國有","s":"Some politicians want to nationalise the power companies, while others believe private competition keeps prices lower.","t":"有些政治人物想要把電力公司收歸國有，而其他人則相信民間競爭能讓價格更低。"},{"w":"overdependence","p":"n.","d":"relying too much on one thing","c":"過度依賴","s":"Europe's overdependence on imported gas became a problem in 2022, so many countries quickly looked for other suppliers.","t":"歐洲對進口天然氣的過度依賴在2022年成了問題，所以許多國家迅速尋找其他供應商。"},{"w":"payoff","p":"n.","d":"a benefit you get from something you did","c":"回報；好處","s":"The payoff from installing insulation came quickly, because our heating bills fell by almost half that winter.","t":"安裝隔熱材料的回報來得很快，因為那年冬天我們的暖氣費幾乎減少了一半。"},{"w":"per capita","p":"adv.","d":"for each person","c":"每人；人均","s":"Americans use much more energy per capita than people in most other countries, because their homes and cars are larger.","t":"美國人的人均能源使用量遠高於大多數其他國家的人，因為他們的房子和車子比較大。"},{"w":"phased","p":"adj.","d":"done gradually in stages","c":"分階段的","s":"The government announced a phased plan to close coal plants, so workers will have time to train for new jobs.","t":"政府宣布了分階段關閉燃煤電廠的計畫，所以工人將有時間接受新工作的訓練。"},{"w":"policymaker","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes government plans and rules","c":"政策制定者","s":"policymaker must balance cheap energy and clean air, but it is not easy to satisfy both goals at once.","t":"政策制定者必須在廉價能源與乾淨空氣之間取得平衡，但同時滿足兩個目標並不容易。"},{"w":"price-sensitive","p":"adj.","d":"likely to change behaviour when prices change","c":"對價格敏感的","s":"Many customers are price-sensitive, so they quickly switch to a cheaper electricity supplier when they see a better offer.","t":"許多顧客對價格敏感，所以一看到更好的方案就會迅速換到更便宜的電力供應商。"},{"w":"privatise","p":"v.","d":"to sell a state-owned company to private owners","c":"民營化","s":"The country decided to privatise its water company, but many citizens were worried that prices would rise.","t":"這個國家決定將水公司民營化，但許多市民擔心價格會上漲。"},{"w":"privatisation","p":"n.","d":"the selling of state-owned companies to private owners","c":"民營化","s":"privatisation of the railways was meant to improve service, but many passengers say trains have become more expensive.","t":"鐵路的民營化原本是為了改善服務，但許多乘客說火車變得更貴了。"},{"w":"projected","p":"adj.","d":"expected based on current information","c":"預計的","s":"The projected cost of the new reactor has doubled, so some lawmakers want to cancel the project.","t":"新反應爐的預計成本已經翻倍，所以有些立法委員想要取消這項計畫。"},{"w":"reallocation","p":"n.","d":"moving resources to a different use","c":"重新分配","s":"The reallocation of money from roads to public transport was popular with students, because buses became cheaper and more frequent.","t":"把經費從道路重新分配到大眾運輸很受學生歡迎，因為公車變得更便宜、班次也更多。"},{"w":"reassessment","p":"n.","d":"the act of judging something again","c":"重新評估","s":"After the earthquake, there was a full reassessment of nuclear safety, and some old plants were closed for good.","t":"地震之後，核能安全被全面重新評估，一些老舊電廠永久關閉。"},{"w":"recyclable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be recycled","c":"可回收的","s":"Most parts of a solar panel are recyclable, so old panels do not have to end up in landfill.","t":"太陽能板大部分零件都是可回收的，所以舊面板不必最後進入掩埋場。"},{"w":"regenerative","p":"adj.","d":"able to recover energy that would be lost","c":"再生的；回充的","s":"Electric cars use regenerative braking, so some energy is returned to the battery every time the driver slows down.","t":"電動車使用再生煞車，所以每次駕駛減速時都會有一些能量回充到電池。"},{"w":"reinvestment","p":"n.","d":"putting profits back into a business or project","c":"再投資","s":"reinvestment of oil profits into schools and hospitals has helped Norway, so the country is rich and well prepared for the future.","t":"把石油利潤再投資於學校和醫院幫助了挪威，所以這個國家富裕且為未來做好準備。"},{"w":"replaceable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be replaced","c":"可替換的","s":"The phone's battery is easily replaceable, so you can buy a new one instead of throwing the whole phone away.","t":"這支手機的電池很容易替換，所以你可以買新電池，而不必丟掉整支手機。"},{"w":"replenishment","p":"n.","d":"filling something up again","c":"補充","s":"The replenishment of underground water takes many years, so farmers should not pump more than the rain can replace.","t":"地下水的補充需要很多年，所以農民抽取的量不應超過雨水能補回的量。"},{"w":"reusable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used again","c":"可重複使用的","s":"We bring reusable shopping bags to the supermarket, because plastic bags are made from oil and are hard to recycle.","t":"我們帶可重複使用的購物袋去超市，因為塑膠袋是用石油製成的，而且很難回收。"},{"w":"rollout","p":"n.","d":"the introduction of a new product or service to many people","c":"推出；普及","s":"The rollout of smart meters began last year, and now customers can check their electricity use on an app.","t":"智慧電表的推出從去年開始，現在顧客可以在應用程式上查看用電量。"},{"w":"scalability","p":"n.","d":"the ability to grow larger easily","c":"可擴展性","s":"The scalability of the new battery design is uncertain, because making it in large factories may be very expensive.","t":"新電池設計的可擴展性還不確定，因為在大型工廠生產它可能非常昂貴。"},{"w":"self-reliance","p":"n.","d":"depending on your own abilities and resources","c":"自力更生","s":"The island values self-reliance, so it produces its own food and electricity instead of depending on the mainland.","t":"這座島重視自力更生，所以它生產自己的食物和電力，而不依賴本島。"},{"w":"storable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be kept for later use","c":"可儲存的","s":"Unlike sunlight, coal is easily storable, so power plants can keep large piles of it for months.","t":"不像陽光，煤炭很容易儲存，所以電廠可以存放大量煤炭好幾個月。"},{"w":"sufficiency","p":"n.","d":"the state of being enough","c":"充足","s":"The report questioned the sufficiency of the country's gas supplies, because demand in winter could be much higher than expected.","t":"報告質疑國家天然氣供應的充足性，因為冬季需求可能遠高於預期。"},{"w":"tradable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be bought and sold","c":"可交易的","s":"Carbon permits are tradable, so companies that pollute less can sell their extra permits to other firms.","t":"碳排放許可是可交易的，所以污染較少的公司可以把多餘的許可賣給其他公司。"},{"w":"uncertain","p":"adj.","d":"not known or not sure","c":"不確定的","s":"The future of the coal mine is uncertain, so many young people in the town are moving to the city for work.","t":"這座煤礦的未來不確定，所以鎮上許多年輕人搬到城市找工作。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 5 (underinvestment – decarbonisation)","cards":[{"w":"underinvestment","p":"n.","d":"not spending enough money on something","c":"投資不足","s":"Years of underinvestment in the power grid led to frequent blackouts, so the government finally promised a large budget.","t":"電網多年來投資不足導致頻繁停電，所以政府終於承諾編列大筆預算。"},{"w":"underused","p":"adj.","d":"not used as much as it could be","c":"未充分利用的","s":"Many school roofs are underused, so the city wants to cover them with solar panels to produce clean power.","t":"許多學校屋頂都未被充分利用，所以市政府想在上面鋪設太陽能板來生產乾淨電力。"},{"w":"unlimited","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit","c":"無限的","s":"Some phone plans offer unlimited data, but streaming videos all day still uses a lot of energy in data centres.","t":"有些手機方案提供無限流量，但整天串流影片仍會在資料中心消耗大量能源。"},{"w":"unrestricted","p":"adj.","d":"not limited by rules","c":"不受限制的","s":"unrestricted pumping of groundwater has caused the land to sink, so new rules now limit how much farmers can take.","t":"不受限制的抽取地下水造成地層下陷，所以新規定現在限制農民可以抽取的量。"},{"w":"usable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used","c":"可用的","s":"Only about a third of the energy in coal becomes usable electricity, while the rest is lost as heat.","t":"煤炭中只有大約三分之一的能量變成可用的電力，其餘都以熱的形式散失。"},{"w":"wastage","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that is wasted","c":"浪費量；損耗","s":"The report showed huge wastage of water in old pipes, so the city plans to repair leaks across every district.","t":"報告顯示老舊水管有大量的水損耗，所以市政府計畫修理每個區域的漏水。"},{"w":"widen","p":"v.","d":"to become or make wider","c":"擴大","s":"The gap between rich and poor may widen if energy prices keep rising, because poor families spend more of their income on bills.","t":"如果能源價格持續上漲，貧富差距可能會擴大，因為貧窮家庭把更多收入花在帳單上。"},{"w":"additional","p":"adj.","d":"extra or more","c":"額外的","s":"The factory needed additional power for its new machines, so it installed solar panels on all its roofs.","t":"工廠的新機器需要額外的電力，所以它在所有屋頂上都裝了太陽能板。"},{"w":"aridity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being very dry","c":"乾燥；乾旱","s":"The aridity of the desert makes farming difficult, but it is an excellent place for solar power because it rarely rains.","t":"沙漠的乾燥讓農耕困難，但因為很少下雨，那裡是發展太陽能的絕佳地點。"},{"w":"authorised","p":"adj.","d":"officially allowed","c":"經授權的","s":"Only authorised workers may enter the power station, so visitors must wear a pass and stay with a guide.","t":"只有經授權的工作人員可以進入發電廠，所以訪客必須配戴通行證並跟著導覽員。"},{"w":"backward","p":"adj.","d":"not developed or modern","c":"落後的","s":"Some people called the village backward because it had no electricity, but now it is a model of solar power.","t":"有些人說這個村莊落後，因為它沒有電，但現在它是太陽能的典範。"},{"w":"brink","p":"n.","d":"the point just before something bad happens","c":"邊緣","s":"The power grid was on the brink of collapse during the heatwave, so the government asked offices to turn off their lights.","t":"熱浪期間電網瀕臨崩潰邊緣，所以政府要求辦公室關燈。"},{"w":"calculable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be worked out with numbers","c":"可計算的","s":"The savings from new windows are easily calculable, so the salesman showed us exactly how much we would save each year.","t":"新窗戶省下的錢很容易計算，所以業務員讓我們清楚看到每年能省多少。"},{"w":"chronologically","p":"adv.","d":"in the order in which events happened","c":"依時間順序地","s":"Our history project lists energy inventions chronologically, starting with the water wheel and ending with modern solar cells.","t":"我們的歷史專題依時間順序列出能源發明，從水車開始，到現代太陽能電池結束。"},{"w":"coefficient","p":"n.","d":"a number that measures a particular quality","c":"係數","s":"Engineers check the heat coefficient of each window, because a lower number means less heat escapes from the house.","t":"工程師會檢查每扇窗戶的傳熱係數，因為數字越低代表從房子散失的熱越少。"},{"w":"commercialisation","p":"n.","d":"turning an invention into a product that is sold","c":"商業化","s":"The commercialisation of hydrogen cars has been slow, because there are very few places where drivers can refuel.","t":"氫能車的商業化一直很緩慢，因為駕駛可以加氫的地方非常少。"},{"w":"competing","p":"adj.","d":"trying to get the same thing as others","c":"相互競爭的","s":"There are competing demands for river water, because farmers, factories and cities all need it in the dry season.","t":"河水有相互競爭的需求，因為農民、工廠和城市在乾季都需要它。"},{"w":"concentrated","p":"adj.","d":"gathered closely in one place","c":"集中的","s":"Most of the world's oil is concentrated in a few regions, so problems there can affect prices everywhere.","t":"世界上大部分石油都集中在少數幾個地區，所以那裡出問題就會影響各地的價格。"},{"w":"condition","p":"n.","d":"something that must happen before something else can happen","c":"條件","s":"The bank agreed to give the loan, but only on the condition that the factory would cut its pollution by half.","t":"銀行同意提供貸款，但條件是工廠必須將污染減半。"},{"w":"constrained","p":"adj.","d":"limited or restricted","c":"受限的","s":"Our school budget is constrained this year, so we cannot buy new air conditioners and must use fans instead.","t":"我們學校今年的預算受限，所以我們不能買新冷氣，只好改用電風扇。"},{"w":"corrosive","p":"adj.","d":"able to slowly damage metal or other materials","c":"腐蝕性的","s":"Sea water is very corrosive, so offshore wind turbines need special paint to protect them from rust.","t":"海水具有很強的腐蝕性，所以離岸風機需要特殊塗料保護以防生鏽。"},{"w":"counterweight","p":"n.","d":"something that balances another force or influence","c":"制衡力量；平衡物","s":"Strong local groups act as a counterweight to big energy companies, so residents' voices are heard before new projects begin.","t":"強大的地方團體是大型能源公司的制衡力量，所以新計畫開始前居民的聲音會被聽見。"},{"w":"crucially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is extremely important","c":"至關重要地","s":"The new battery is cheaper, and crucially, it can be charged in only ten minutes, so drivers will not have to wait long.","t":"新電池比較便宜，而且最關鍵的是，它只要十分鐘就能充好電，所以駕駛不必等很久。"},{"w":"customised","p":"adj.","d":"made for a particular person or need","c":"量身訂製的","s":"The company offers customised energy plans, so each family pays for the kind of power it actually uses.","t":"這家公司提供量身訂製的能源方案，所以每個家庭只為實際使用的電力付費。"},{"w":"decarbonisation","p":"n.","d":"reducing the carbon dioxide produced by an activity","c":"去碳化；減碳","s":"decarbonisation of the steel industry is difficult, because making steel usually needs very high heat from coal.","t":"鋼鐵業的去碳化很困難，因為煉鋼通常需要來自煤炭的極高溫。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 6 (decentralisation – intergovernmental)","cards":[{"w":"decentralisation","p":"n.","d":"moving power or control away from one centre","c":"分散化","s":"The decentralisation of electricity production lets families sell solar power, so they become producers as well as customers.","t":"電力生產的分散化讓家庭可以出售太陽能電力，所以他們既是顧客也是生產者。"},{"w":"deflation","p":"n.","d":"a general fall in prices in an economy","c":"通貨緊縮","s":"The country faced deflation after oil prices dropped, so shops kept cutting prices and companies earned less.","t":"油價下跌後這個國家面臨通貨緊縮，所以商店不斷降價，公司的收入也減少了。"},{"w":"depreciate","p":"v.","d":"to lose value over time","c":"貶值；折舊","s":"Electric cars used to depreciate quickly, but now buyers trust the batteries more, so used ones keep their value better.","t":"電動車過去貶值很快，但現在買家比較信任電池，所以二手車更能保值。"},{"w":"destabilising","p":"adj.","d":"making a situation less steady or safe","c":"造成不穩定的","s":"Sudden changes in oil prices can be destabilising for poor countries, because they cannot easily pay for fuel imports.","t":"油價的突然變動對貧窮國家可能造成不穩定，因為它們無法輕易支付燃料進口費用。"},{"w":"devolution","p":"n.","d":"passing power from central government to local areas","c":"權力下放","s":"devolution of energy decisions to cities has worked well, because local leaders understand their residents' needs better.","t":"將能源決策權力下放給城市成效良好，因為地方領袖更了解居民的需求。"},{"w":"diffuse","p":"adj.","d":"spread over a large area, not concentrated","c":"分散的；擴散的","s":"Sunlight is a diffuse source of energy, so we need large areas of panels to collect enough of it.","t":"陽光是分散的能源，所以我們需要大面積的太陽能板才能收集足夠的能量。"},{"w":"dilution","p":"n.","d":"making something weaker by adding something else","c":"稀釋；削弱","s":"Environmental groups complained about the dilution of the new law, because many of its strict rules were removed.","t":"環保團體抱怨新法遭到削弱，因為許多嚴格規定被刪除了。"},{"w":"diminished","p":"adj.","d":"made smaller or weaker","c":"減弱的","s":"The dam has a diminished ability to produce power in summer, because the river carries much less water then.","t":"這座水壩夏季的發電能力減弱，因為那時河水流量少了很多。"},{"w":"directive","p":"n.","d":"an official instruction","c":"指令；命令","s":"The ministry issued a new directive last week, and all public buildings must now keep air conditioning above 26 degrees.","t":"部會上週發布了一項新指令，所有公共建築現在必須將冷氣溫度維持在26度以上。"},{"w":"downgrade","p":"v.","d":"to lower the level or importance of something","c":"降低；下修","s":"The bank had to downgrade its forecast for the energy company, because the new gas field produced less than expected.","t":"銀行不得不下修對這家能源公司的預測，因為新氣田的產量低於預期。"},{"w":"downstream","p":"adv.","d":"further along a river, towards its end","c":"在下游","s":"Pollution from the mine travelled downstream, so villages many kilometres away could no longer use the river for drinking.","t":"礦場的污染流向下游，所以許多公里外的村莊再也無法飲用河水。"},{"w":"electorate","p":"n.","d":"all the people allowed to vote","c":"選民","s":"The electorate voted against the new nuclear plant, so the government had to look for other ways to produce power.","t":"選民投票反對新核電廠，所以政府必須尋找其他發電方式。"},{"w":"encroachment","p":"n.","d":"slowly taking over land or rights","c":"侵占；侵蝕","s":"The encroachment of mines onto farmland has angered villagers, because they are losing the fields their families farmed for generations.","t":"礦場對農地的侵占激怒了村民，因為他們正失去家族世代耕種的田地。"},{"w":"enlargement","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something bigger","c":"擴大；擴建","s":"The enlargement of the port will allow bigger gas ships to arrive, but fishermen worry about losing their fishing areas.","t":"港口的擴建將讓更大的天然氣船能夠進港，但漁民擔心失去漁場。"},{"w":"entrench","p":"v.","d":"to fix an idea or system firmly so it is hard to change","c":"使根深蒂固","s":"Cheap coal can entrench old habits, so countries may find it harder to move to cleaner energy later.","t":"廉價煤炭可能讓舊習慣根深蒂固，所以各國日後可能更難轉向更乾淨的能源。"},{"w":"exportable","p":"adj.","d":"suitable for selling to other countries","c":"可出口的","s":"The country produces more gas than it needs, so the extra is exportable and brings in a lot of money.","t":"這個國家生產的天然氣多於所需，所以多餘的部分可以出口，帶來大量收入。"},{"w":"externality","p":"n.","d":"a cost or benefit that affects people outside a business","c":"外部性","s":"Air pollution is a negative externality of coal power, because people living nearby suffer but do not get paid for it.","t":"空氣污染是燃煤發電的負面外部性，因為住在附近的人受害卻沒有得到補償。"},{"w":"footprint","p":"n.","d":"the amount of space or effect something has","c":"足跡；占用面積","s":"The new solar farm has a large footprint, so the designers placed it on an old landfill instead of on farmland.","t":"新的太陽能發電場占地很大，所以設計師把它設在舊掩埋場而不是農地上。"},{"w":"overcapacity","p":"n.","d":"having more ability to produce than is needed","c":"產能過剩","s":"There is overcapacity in the solar panel industry, so many factories are selling panels at very low prices.","t":"太陽能板產業產能過剩，所以許多工廠以非常低的價格出售面板。"},{"w":"fractured","p":"adj.","d":"broken or split","c":"破裂的；分裂的","s":"The fractured pipe leaked oil into the river for hours, but workers finally managed to shut off the flow.","t":"破裂的管線把石油漏進河裡好幾個小時，但工人最後終於成功止漏。"},{"w":"generational","p":"adj.","d":"related to different age groups","c":"世代的","s":"There is a generational difference in attitudes to energy, because young people care more about climate change than their grandparents.","t":"人們對能源的態度存在世代差異，因為年輕人比他們的祖父母更在乎氣候變遷。"},{"w":"heightened","p":"adj.","d":"made stronger or greater","c":"升高的；加強的","s":"There is heightened security at the gas terminal after the warning, so every truck is checked before it enters.","t":"收到警告後，天然氣接收站的安全戒備升高，所以每輛卡車進入前都要接受檢查。"},{"w":"import-dependent","p":"adj.","d":"relying on goods from other countries","c":"依賴進口的","s":"Japan is highly import-dependent for energy, so it keeps large stores of oil in case supplies are cut.","t":"日本在能源上高度依賴進口，所以它儲備大量石油以防供應中斷。"},{"w":"inflow","p":"n.","d":"movement of something into a place","c":"流入","s":"The inflow of foreign money into wind projects has created jobs, and local factories now make turbine parts.","t":"外國資金流入風電計畫創造了就業，當地工廠現在也生產風機零件。"},{"w":"intergovernmental","p":"adj.","d":"between or involving several governments","c":"政府間的","s":"An intergovernmental meeting was held to discuss shared rivers, because the dams in one country affect water in the others.","t":"為了討論共享河流舉行了一場政府間會議，因為一國的水壩會影響其他國家的水源。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 7 (interruption – prospecting)","cards":[{"w":"interruption","p":"n.","d":"a break in a service or activity","c":"中斷","s":"There will be a short interruption to the water supply tomorrow morning, so please fill some bottles tonight.","t":"明天早上供水將短暫中斷，所以請今晚先裝好幾瓶水。"},{"w":"irreplaceable","p":"adj.","d":"too special or rare to be replaced","c":"無可取代的","s":"The wetland is irreplaceable for migrating birds, so scientists strongly opposed plans to build a gas terminal there.","t":"這片濕地對候鳥來說是無可取代的，所以科學家強烈反對在那裡興建天然氣接收站。"},{"w":"irreversibly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that cannot be changed back","c":"不可逆地","s":"The mine has irreversibly changed the shape of the mountain, so the old hiking trail can never be restored.","t":"這座礦場已經不可逆地改變了山的形狀，所以舊登山步道再也無法恢復。"},{"w":"jeopardy","p":"n.","d":"danger of loss or harm","c":"危險；危難","s":"Thousands of jobs are in jeopardy because the coal plant is closing, so the town is looking for new industries.","t":"由於燃煤電廠即將關閉，數千個工作陷入危險，所以鎮上正在尋找新的產業。"},{"w":"landlocked","p":"adj.","d":"surrounded by land, with no coast","c":"內陸的","s":"The country is landlocked and has no ports, so it must send its oil through pipelines across other countries to reach the sea.","t":"這個國家是內陸國，沒有港口，所以它必須透過穿越其他國家的管線把石油送到海邊。"},{"w":"lead time","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time between starting something and finishing it","c":"前置時間","s":"Nuclear plants have a long lead time, so a plant planned today may not produce power for over ten years.","t":"核電廠的前置時間很長，所以今天規劃的電廠可能要十多年後才能發電。"},{"w":"leakage","p":"n.","d":"the escape of liquid or gas through a hole","c":"洩漏","s":"Methane leakage from old gas pipes is a serious problem, because this gas traps much more heat than carbon dioxide.","t":"老舊天然氣管線的甲烷洩漏是嚴重問題，因為這種氣體比二氧化碳吸收更多熱。"},{"w":"legislate","p":"v.","d":"to make laws","c":"立法","s":"Parliament plans to legislate against selling new petrol cars after 2035, but car makers have asked for more time.","t":"國會計畫立法禁止在2035年後販售新的汽油車，但汽車製造商要求更多時間。"},{"w":"lifetime","p":"n.","d":"the period of time something lasts","c":"壽命","s":"Solar panels have a lifetime of about twenty-five years, so they continue producing power long after their cost is paid back.","t":"太陽能板的壽命大約二十五年，所以在回本之後仍會持續發電很久。"},{"w":"long-run","p":"adj.","d":"relating to a long period of time","c":"長期的","s":"The long-run benefits of insulation are clear, but many landlords do not want to pay the cost today.","t":"隔熱的長期好處很明顯，但許多房東不想現在付出成本。"},{"w":"marginalise","p":"v.","d":"to treat a person or group as unimportant","c":"邊緣化","s":"Big energy projects sometimes marginalise local communities, because decisions are made in the capital without asking them.","t":"大型能源計畫有時會把地方社區邊緣化，因為決策在首都做出而沒有詢問他們。"},{"w":"moratorium","p":"n.","d":"an official stop to an activity for a time","c":"暫停令","s":"The government placed a moratorium on new coal mines, so no new projects can start for the next five years.","t":"政府對新煤礦下了暫停令，所以未來五年都不能啟動新計畫。"},{"w":"multilateral","p":"adj.","d":"involving three or more countries","c":"多邊的","s":"A multilateral agreement was signed to protect the river, because it flows through four different countries.","t":"為了保護這條河，各國簽署了一項多邊協議，因為它流經四個不同國家。"},{"w":"neutrality","p":"n.","d":"the state of not causing a particular effect","c":"中和；中立","s":"The city aims to reach carbon neutrality by 2050, so it is planting trees and switching buses to electric power.","t":"這座城市目標在2050年達成碳中和，所以它正在植樹並把公車改為電動。"},{"w":"onshore","p":"adj.","d":"on land rather than at sea","c":"陸上的","s":"onshore wind farms are cheaper to build, but people living nearby sometimes complain about the noise and the view.","t":"陸上風場建造成本較低，但附近居民有時會抱怨噪音和景觀。"},{"w":"outflow","p":"n.","d":"movement of something out of a place","c":"流出","s":"There was a large outflow of money from oil companies last year, because investors moved their money into clean energy.","t":"去年石油公司出現大量資金流出，因為投資人把錢轉移到乾淨能源。"},{"w":"outsourcing","p":"n.","d":"paying another company to do work for you","c":"外包","s":"The outsourcing of battery production to other countries saved money, but it also made the car industry less secure.","t":"把電池生產外包到其他國家省下了錢，但也讓汽車產業變得較不安全。"},{"w":"payback period","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time it takes for savings to repay the cost","c":"回收期","s":"The payback period for rooftop solar is about seven years, so after that the family gets almost free electricity.","t":"屋頂太陽能的回收期大約七年，所以之後這個家庭幾乎可以免費用電。"},{"w":"penetration","p":"n.","d":"how far something has spread into a market","c":"普及率；滲透率","s":"The penetration of electric cars in Norway is very high, so most new cars sold there are now electric.","t":"挪威的電動車普及率非常高，所以那裡賣出的新車現在大多是電動車。"},{"w":"phase-out","p":"n.","d":"the gradual ending of something","c":"逐步淘汰","s":"The phase-out of coal will take many years, because the country still depends on it for much of its electricity.","t":"煤炭的逐步淘汰將需要很多年，因為這個國家仍有大量電力依賴它。"},{"w":"pilot","p":"adj.","d":"done on a small scale as a test","c":"試驗性的；先導的","s":"The city started a pilot project with electric scooters, and if it succeeds, the programme will spread to every district.","t":"市政府啟動了一項電動機車的先導計畫，如果成功，這個方案將推廣到每個區域。"},{"w":"polarised","p":"adj.","d":"divided into two strongly opposing groups","c":"兩極化的","s":"Opinion on nuclear power is very polarised, so it is hard for the government to make a decision everyone accepts.","t":"對核能的意見非常兩極化，所以政府很難做出人人都接受的決定。"},{"w":"predictability","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being expected or known in advance","c":"可預測性","s":"Investors value the predictability of tidal power, because the tides follow a clear pattern every day.","t":"投資人重視潮汐發電的可預測性，因為潮汐每天都遵循清楚的規律。"},{"w":"price ceiling","p":"n.phr.","d":"the highest price allowed by law","c":"價格上限","s":"The government set a price ceiling on cooking gas, so poor families could still afford to cook during the crisis.","t":"政府對烹飪用瓦斯設定了價格上限，所以貧窮家庭在危機期間仍能負擔得起煮飯。"},{"w":"prospecting","p":"n.","d":"searching an area for gold, oil or minerals","c":"探勘","s":"prospecting for lithium has started in the desert, and many people hope it will bring jobs to the poor region.","t":"沙漠中已經開始探勘鋰礦，許多人希望它能為這個貧窮地區帶來工作。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"Academic Words 學術單字 8 (protectionist – worsening)","cards":[{"w":"protectionist","p":"adj.","d":"protecting local industry by limiting foreign goods","c":"保護主義的","s":"protectionist policies made imported solar panels more expensive, so local factories sold more but customers paid higher prices.","t":"保護主義政策讓進口太陽能板變貴，所以本地工廠賣得更多，但消費者付了更高的價格。"},{"w":"rebound effect","p":"n.phr.","d":"when saving energy leads people to use more","c":"反彈效應","s":"Because of the rebound effect, some people drive more after buying an efficient car, so the total fuel saved is smaller.","t":"由於反彈效應，有些人買了省油車之後開得更多，所以總共省下的燃料變少了。"},{"w":"reclamation","p":"n.","d":"making damaged land useful again","c":"復育；再利用","s":"Land reclamation after mining takes years, but the old coal site is now a park with lakes and walking paths.","t":"採礦後的土地復育需要好幾年，但舊煤礦場現在已成為有湖泊和步道的公園。"},{"w":"recoverable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be taken out or got back","c":"可回收的；可開採的","s":"Experts say only half of the oil in the field is recoverable, because the rest is trapped too deep in the rock.","t":"專家說這座油田只有一半的石油可開採，因為其餘的被困在岩層太深處。"},{"w":"relocation","p":"n.","d":"moving to a new place","c":"遷移；搬遷","s":"The relocation of families from the dam area was painful, because many had lived in the valley for generations.","t":"水壩區家庭的遷移令人痛苦，因為許多人世代居住在這座山谷。"},{"w":"remediation","p":"n.","d":"the process of cleaning up polluted land or water","c":"整治；修復","s":"Soil remediation at the old factory site will cost millions, so the government is asking the company to pay.","t":"舊工廠廠址的土壤整治將耗資數百萬，所以政府要求公司付費。"},{"w":"renegotiation","p":"n.","d":"discussing an agreement again to change it","c":"重新談判","s":"The renegotiation of the gas contract took months, but in the end both countries agreed on a lower price.","t":"天然氣合約的重新談判花了好幾個月，但最後兩國同意了較低的價格。"},{"w":"reversible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed back","c":"可逆的","s":"Some damage from mining is reversible, so planting trees and cleaning rivers can help the land recover.","t":"有些採礦造成的破壞是可逆的，所以種樹和清理河川能幫助土地復原。"},{"w":"slowdown","p":"n.","d":"a reduction in speed or activity","c":"減緩；放緩","s":"An economic slowdown reduced factory output, so electricity demand fell for the first time in ten years.","t":"經濟放緩使工廠產量減少，所以電力需求十年來首次下降。"},{"w":"sovereign","p":"adj.","d":"having full control over its own affairs","c":"主權的；自主的","s":"Norway put its oil money into a sovereign wealth fund, so future generations will also benefit from the country's resources.","t":"挪威把石油收入放進主權財富基金，所以未來世代也能從國家資源中受益。"},{"w":"spillover","p":"n.","d":"an effect that spreads beyond its original area","c":"外溢效應","s":"The new battery factory had a positive spillover on the town, because restaurants and shops got more customers.","t":"新電池工廠對小鎮產生了正面的外溢效應，因為餐廳和商店有了更多客人。"},{"w":"standstill","p":"n.","d":"a situation with no movement or progress","c":"停頓；停滯","s":"The strike brought the oil refinery to a standstill, so petrol stations soon began to run out of fuel.","t":"罷工讓煉油廠陷入停頓，所以加油站很快就開始缺油。"},{"w":"taxpayer","p":"n.","d":"a person who pays tax","c":"納稅人","s":"taxpayer will pay for cleaning up the old mine, because the mining company went bankrupt years ago.","t":"納稅人將支付清理舊礦場的費用，因為那家採礦公司多年前就破產了。"},{"w":"tighten","p":"v.","d":"to make rules stricter","c":"收緊；加強","s":"The government plans to tighten the rules on factory pollution, so companies must install cleaner equipment within three years.","t":"政府計畫加強工廠污染規範，所以公司必須在三年內安裝更乾淨的設備。"},{"w":"transnational","p":"adj.","d":"operating across several countries","c":"跨國的","s":"A transnational energy company owns power plants in ten countries, so its decisions affect millions of customers.","t":"一家跨國能源公司在十個國家擁有電廠，所以它的決策影響數百萬名顧客。"},{"w":"unabated","p":"adj.","d":"continuing without becoming weaker","c":"有增無減的","s":"Demand for air conditioning has continued unabated, so power companies must keep building new capacity.","t":"冷氣需求持續有增無減，所以電力公司必須不斷擴建新的發電容量。"},{"w":"uncontrollable","p":"adj.","d":"impossible to control","c":"無法控制的","s":"The fire at the oil depot became uncontrollable, so firefighters had to evacuate everyone living within two kilometres.","t":"油庫的火勢變得無法控制，所以消防員必須疏散兩公里內的所有居民。"},{"w":"underground","p":"adv.","d":"below the surface of the ground","c":"在地下","s":"The city put its power lines underground, so typhoons no longer knock down cables and cause blackouts.","t":"市政府把電線埋在地下，所以颱風不再吹倒電纜造成停電。"},{"w":"unexploited","p":"adj.","d":"not yet used or developed","c":"未開發的","s":"Africa has huge unexploited solar potential, so investors believe it could become a major producer of clean power.","t":"非洲擁有巨大的未開發太陽能潛力，所以投資人相信它可能成為乾淨電力的主要生產地。"},{"w":"unrelenting","p":"adj.","d":"continuing strongly without stopping","c":"持續不斷的","s":"The unrelenting heat lasted for two weeks, so the power company asked people to avoid using washing machines in the afternoon.","t":"持續不斷的高溫延續了兩週，所以電力公司要求民眾避免在下午使用洗衣機。"},{"w":"unsustainably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that cannot continue for a long time","c":"不可持續地","s":"Groundwater is being used unsustainably in this region, so the wells may be completely dry within twenty years.","t":"這個地區的地下水正被不可持續地使用，所以水井可能在二十年內完全乾涸。"},{"w":"upstream","p":"adv.","d":"towards the beginning of a river","c":"在上游","s":"A new dam was built upstream, so the farmers downstream now receive much less water for their crops.","t":"上游蓋了一座新水壩，所以下游的農民現在得到的灌溉用水少了很多。"},{"w":"upward","p":"adj.","d":"moving towards a higher level","c":"向上的","s":"There has been an upward trend in electricity prices, so families are looking for ways to cut their use.","t":"電價呈現上升趨勢，所以家庭都在尋找減少用電的方法。"},{"w":"vested interest","p":"n.phr.","d":"a personal reason for wanting something to happen","c":"既得利益","s":"Oil companies have a vested interest in keeping petrol cars on the road, so they sometimes oppose new electric car policies.","t":"石油公司在讓汽油車繼續上路方面有既得利益，所以它們有時會反對新的電動車政策。"},{"w":"worsening","p":"adj.","d":"becoming worse","c":"日益惡化的","s":"The worsening water shortage forced the city to reduce water pressure at night, so some tall buildings had no water.","t":"日益惡化的缺水迫使市政府在夜間降低水壓，所以一些高樓沒有水。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"Fixed Phrases & Collocations 固定片語與搭配詞","cards":[{"w":"run on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use something as fuel or power","c":"以…為動力","s":"Our new school bus run on electricity, so it is much quieter and the students no longer breathe in diesel smoke.","t":"我們的新校車以電力為動力，所以安靜許多，學生也不再吸到柴油廢氣。"},{"w":"keep the lights on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep the power supply or a business running","c":"維持供電；維持運作","s":"During the storm, engineers worked all night to keep the lights on, and the city did not lose power.","t":"暴風雨期間，工程師整夜工作以維持供電，所以城市沒有停電。"},{"w":"tap into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make use of a supply of something","c":"利用；開發","s":"Many countries want to tap into the strong winds at sea, so they are building large offshore wind farms.","t":"許多國家想要利用海上的強風，所以它們正在興建大型離岸風場。"},{"w":"a drain on","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that uses up money or resources","c":"消耗；負擔","s":"The old air conditioner is a drain on our money, so we have decided to replace it with a more efficient one.","t":"那台舊冷氣是我們金錢上的一大負擔，所以我們決定換一台更省電的。"},{"w":"run dry","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no water or supply left","c":"乾涸；耗盡","s":"The wells in the village began to run dry during the long drought, so families had to buy water from trucks.","t":"長期乾旱期間村裡的井開始乾涸，所以家家戶戶只好向水車買水。"},{"w":"add fuel to the fire","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a bad situation even worse","c":"火上加油","s":"The minister's rude comment about protesters only add fuel to the fire, and even more people joined the march.","t":"部長對抗議者的無禮言論只是火上加油，結果更多人加入遊行。"},{"w":"run low on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have only a small amount of something left","c":"快用完","s":"We were run low on petrol in the mountains, so we drove slowly and looked anxiously for a station.","t":"我們在山區時汽油快用完了，所以我們慢慢開，焦急地尋找加油站。"},{"w":"strike gold","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly find something very valuable or successful","c":"挖到寶；大獲成功","s":"The small company strike gold with its cheap solar lamp, because millions of families without electricity wanted one.","t":"這家小公司以便宜的太陽能燈大獲成功，因為數百萬個沒有電的家庭都想要一盞。"},{"w":"recharge one's batteries","p":"v.phr.","d":"to rest so you have energy again","c":"養精蓄銳；充電","s":"I spent the weekend in the mountains to recharge one's batteries, and I felt ready to study hard again on Monday.","t":"我週末去山上養精蓄銳，星期一就覺得準備好再次努力讀書了。"},{"w":"make the switch to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change from one thing to another","c":"改用；轉換到","s":"Our family decided to make the switch to an electric scooter, because petrol was getting too expensive.","t":"我們家決定改用電動機車，因為汽油變得太貴了。"},{"w":"low-hanging fruit","p":"n.phr.","d":"the easiest things to do or achieve first","c":"容易達成的目標","s":"Turning off unused lights is low-hanging fruit, so our school started with that before installing solar panels.","t":"關掉沒在用的燈是容易達成的目標，所以我們學校在安裝太陽能板前先從這件事做起。"},{"w":"scrape the bottom of the barrel","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use the worst things because nothing better is left","c":"退而求其次；別無選擇只能用最差的","s":"The country was scrape the bottom of the barrel by burning dirty coal, because it had run out of cleaner fuels.","t":"這個國家只能退而求其次燃燒骯髒的煤，因為它已經用光了更乾淨的燃料。"},{"w":"burn the candle at both ends","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work very hard and sleep too little","c":"蠟燭兩頭燒","s":"My sister has been burn the candle at both ends before her exams, so she looks tired and often gets headaches.","t":"我姊姊考試前一直蠟燭兩頭燒，所以她看起來很疲倦，常常頭痛。"},{"w":"pull the plug on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop an activity or project","c":"叫停；終止","s":"The government decided to pull the plug on the new coal plant, because the costs were too high and many people opposed it.","t":"政府決定叫停新的燃煤電廠，因為成本太高，而且許多人反對。"},{"w":"running on empty","p":"adj.phr.","d":"having no energy or resources left","c":"筋疲力盡；油盡燈枯","s":"After working three night shifts in a row, the nurse was running on empty, so she went straight to bed.","t":"連續上了三個夜班之後，那位護理師已經筋疲力盡，所以她直接上床睡覺。"},{"w":"worth its weight in gold","p":"adj.phr.","d":"extremely useful or valuable","c":"非常珍貴","s":"During the typhoon our small generator was worth its weight in gold, because it kept the fridge and lights working.","t":"颱風期間我們的小發電機非常珍貴，因為它讓冰箱和電燈持續運作。"},{"w":"dig deep","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use all your strength or money for something","c":"竭盡全力；慷慨解囊","s":"Residents had to dig deep to pay for repairs after the flood, but neighbours also helped each other generously.","t":"水災後居民必須竭盡全力支付修繕費用，但鄰居之間也慷慨地互相幫忙。"},{"w":"go up in smoke","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fail or be destroyed completely","c":"化為泡影；付之一炬","s":"Our plans for a beach holiday go up in smoke when petrol prices doubled, so we stayed home instead.","t":"當油價翻倍時，我們去海邊度假的計畫化為泡影，所以我們改成待在家裡。"},{"w":"plug the gap","p":"v.phr.","d":"to provide something that is missing","c":"填補缺口","s":"When the nuclear plant closed, gas power was used to plug the gap, but it made electricity more expensive.","t":"核電廠關閉時，燃氣發電被用來填補缺口，但這讓電價變得更貴。"},{"w":"at full blast","p":"phr.","d":"as strongly or loudly as possible","c":"開到最大","s":"My brother had the air conditioner at full blast all afternoon, so my parents were shocked when the electricity bill arrived.","t":"我弟弟整個下午把冷氣開到最大，所以電費帳單寄來時我父母都嚇了一跳。"}]}];
